{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dnur6NE8txUsVaL41S2Yc9","type":"tool_result","content":"1000\t| `pavilionClock`, `veranda` | pavilion details | green |\n1001\t| `teaUrn`, `teapot`, `cakeStand` | tea-room set (with the store's cakes) | cutscenes |\n1002\t| `deckchair` | striped canvas deck chair (3 colourways) | green, hall, bay |\n1003\t| `umbrellaOpen` | crowd umbrella (rain) | downs |\n1004\t| `covers` | blue tarpaulin over the pitch, rolled or spread (params `spread: 0..1`) | rain delay |\n1005\t| `roller` | heavy groundsman's roller | green, cutscene |\n1006\t| `floodlight` | lattice pylon with a lamp bank (`lights`) | dome, night matches |\n1007\t| `adBoard` | boundary board with a sponsor name painted (params `text`, colours): *Crumb's Cakes*, *Leaning Wicket Ales*, *Thrumpton Holdings*, *Kerfuffle Teas* | all |\n1008\t| `pubFront` | the Leaning Wicket's frontage, with a breakable window sprite | green |\n1009\t| `greenhouse` | the glass-pane vicarage greenhouse (shatterable) | green |\n1010\t| `churchSpire`, `weathervane` | the weathervane spins on hit (`params: { angle }` in 16 steps) | green |\n1011\t| `oakTree` | the big oak inside the boundary (a large `tree` variant), with a beehive | green |\n1012\t| `fountain` | a tiered fountain with water drawn live | hall |\n1013\t| `phantomCar` | Thrumpton's vintage car (original design: long bonnet, running boards) | green, hall |\n1014\t| `peacock` | sprite frames: walk and display fan | hall |\n1015\t| `beachHut` | striped hut | bay |\n1016\t| `pier`, `ferrisWheel` | pier with a Ferris wheel (`params: { angle }` turning) | bay |\n1017\t| `iceCreamVan` | van with a giant cone | bay |\n1018\t| `inflatableShark` | the shark | bay |\n1019\t| `seagull` | sprite frames: flap, glide, carry a ball | bay |\n1020\t| `topHat` | giant magician's top hat on the boundary | downs |\n1021\t| `waterTower` | a timber water tower: a round tank on four braced stilts, with a ladder | downs |\n1022\t| `hotAirBalloon` | drifting on an `E.Path` | downs |\n1023\t| `caravan` | magician's caravan | downs |\n1024\t| `megadomeTier`, `vipBox`, `laserRig`, `ghostBell` | Megadome set | dome |\n1025\t| `thrumptonator` | the steam bowling machine: brass boiler, pipes, a throwing wheel (`params: { angle }`), pressure gauge, smoke from `particles.smoke` | dome, showdown, hub |\n1026\t| `minibus` | the Kerfuffle Express (map and cutscene) | map |\n1027\t| `cow` | Doris: a Friesian built from parts, with leg-swing animation via params (`step: 0..15`) | green |\n1028\t| `coin` | toss coin sprite frames (8) | toss |\n1029\t| `itemTokens` | sprites (16×16): Golden Teapot, Lucky Horseshoe, Giant Bat, Cake Slice, Sticky Gloves, Banana Peel, Fog Machine | items |\n1030\t\n1031\t### 6.6 Effects (`33-fx.js`)\n1032\t- **Ball:** a trail (the last 12 positions, fading), a shadow, a speed-streak for >140 km/h, a glow at night.\n1033\t- **Bat contact:** splinters (`particles.bits`, willow colours) and an impact star on PERFECT.\n1034\t- **Bowled:** stumps knocked back, bails as physics sprites spinning away, a dust burst and a camera shake of 2. With a special: the stumps cartwheel high (over the top) and land in the keeper's hands.\n1035\t- **ON FIRE:** flame particles on the bat or ball (`particles.fire`) with an emissive glow.\n1036\t- **Specials:**\n1037\t  - Tea-Kettle Slog: a steam-whistle trail and steam puffs;\n1038\t  - Vicar's Revenge: a holy-light ray and a choir chord;\n1039\t  - The Grandad: three dust puffs;\n1040\t  - Peregrine Swoop: a feather trail;\n1041\t  - Sunburn Bouncer: heat haze (a row-offset shimmer on the overlay);\n1042\t  - Vanishing Ball: a puff of purple smoke, gone for 0.3 s, then a puff again;\n1043\t  - Triple Threat: two hologram balls (cyan, flickering) and one real one (a seam glint);\n1044\t  - Grudge Ball: a red outline;\n1045\t  - Ectoplasmic Edge: ghost trails.\n1046\t- **Sixes:** the ball lands in the stands with a crowd scatter and a \"crowd catch\" arm. Fireworks on sixes at night (`particles.explosion` small, no shake) and confetti on wins.\n1047\t- **Weather:** rain (engine), puddles on the covers, fog overlay, dust devils (`particles.dust` spirals), drifting cloud shadows.\n1048\t- **Rule:** all effects respect Comfort settings (reduce motion: no shake, shorter flashes).\n1049\t\n1050\t---\n1051\t\n1052\t## 7. Animation (`32-anim.js`)\n1053\tBase: the engine's procedural Humanoid. Build cricket-specific motion from four tools:\n1054\t- **(a)** `E.Attack` specs with custom `a0/a1/z0/z1/reach/hand:'both'/plane/lunge/crouch/lean/twist/hold`, and phases timed so that \"active\" starts at the shot's `contactAt`;\n1055\t- **(b)** poses (`pose`, `expr`, `stance`, `crouch`, `run`, `down`);\n1056\t- **(c)** `rig.solvePose` post-processing (wrap it per rig) to place hands with `E.ik3` for two-handed bat grips, the bowling arm's vertical windmill and umpire signals;\n1057\t- **(d)** `E.ACTIONS` entries for dives, slides and the run turn (`{ beats, setup, at }`).\n1058\t\n1059\tCheck every motion with `node engine/tools/filmstrip.mjs dist/index.html#<scene> --steps \"...\" --seed 1`. Each must wind up, strike and settle back without snapping or sweeping backwards.\n1060\t\n1061\t| Role | Animations |\n1062\t|---|---|\n1063\t| Batter | stance (side-on, knees flexed, bat tapping), trigger step, front-foot and back-foot defence, leave (bat high), duck and sway, drives (straight, cover, on), cut, pull, hook, flick, glance, sweep, slog-sweep, lofted drive, scoop, upper cut, helicopter (a full wrist whirl: bat rotates 360° after contact), charge (2 quick steps), run carrying the bat, the crease turn (an `E.ACTIONS` pivot with the bat grounded), the dive (body flat, bat stretched: `down` plus a lunge), walk-off (`hunch`, slow), celebrations (bat raised for 50 or a six; a bat twirl), dejection (`kneel`) |\n1064\t| Bowler | run-up (pace: accelerating; spin: 4 steps), the bound (a hop), the delivery stride: front arm up, then the bowling arm windmills over the top in the vertical plane, the right hand IK'd round a circle centred on the shoulder (radius = the arm's length) over 0.18 s, with the release at the top front. Then the follow-through (a stoop, then running off to the side of the pitch). A spinner's version is shorter with a wrist flick. Also the appeal (both arms up, `shout`), the aeroplane celebration (arms out, a curved run), a knee slide, hands on head |\n1065\t| Fielders | walking in (crouched), the ready position, chase, slide stop, pick-up, overarm throw (wind back, sling: the `throw` move), underarm flick, the diving catch (an `E.ACTIONS` full-length dive and roll), the high catch (hands cupped above the eyes), juggle, drop, the catch celebration (ball tossed up), backing up |\n1066\t| Keeper | crouch, rise with the ball, catch (gloves up), dive, stumping (whip the bails: a fast hand arc), standing up to spin |\n1067\t| Umpire | stand with hands behind back, slight crouch at delivery. Signals: OUT (finger raised slowly; Rev. Hollis takes 1.2 s), FOUR (arm waved across the chest), SIX (both arms up), WIDE (arms out horizontally), NO BALL (one arm out), BYE (palm up), LEG BYE (touch a raised knee), FREE HIT (circling finger over the head), REVIEW (draws a TV rectangle in the air), DEAD BALL (crossing wrists) |\n1068\t| Others | Thrumpton's sneer and monocle-adjust (a hand to the eye), Mrs Crumb pouring tea, Doris grazing and walking, seagulls flap, the peacock's fan display, ghosts float (a z bob plus alpha flicker), the mascot runner in a chicken costume (a hood plus beak colours) chased by two stewards, the crowd |\n1069\t\n1070\tAnimation tests: filmstrips reviewed (§11.5); and headless checks that every shot's \"active\" phase begins within ±8 ms of its `contactAt`, the bowling hand passes over the head (z > head z) during the stride, and every signal ends back at rest.\n1071\t\n1072\t---\n1073\t\n1074\t## 8. Content\n1075\t\n1076\t### 8.1 Cast (main characters)\n1077\t| Name | Role | Look (rig) | Voice |\n1078\t|---|---|---|---|\n1079\t| **Edie Pluckrose** | Kerfuffle CC captain; fast bowler and big hitter; the vicar's daughter, unflappable | heroic, size 1.2; auburn ponytail; cream kit, green cap and trim; freckles (portrait detail) | 240 Hz, brisk |\n1080\t| **Basil Thwaite** | 74-year-old leg-spinner; claims he once bowled out a duke | chibi, walrus moustache, bald under a faded green cap, cardigan (coat outfit, beige) | 120 Hz wobbly |\n1081\t| **Dev Mistry** | opening batter; leaves everything; quotes statistics | heroic; neat black hair; glasses; helmet | 170 Hz precise |\n1082\t| **Pip Larkin** | teenage keeper; never stops chirping | chibi; spiky blonde hair; oversized gloves | 290 Hz fast |\n1083\t| **Mrs Agatha Crumb** | tea lady, scorer and tactical genius; runs the Nets lessons | chibi; grey bun; floral apron (robe outfit) | 220 Hz warm |\n1084\t| **Rev. Hollis** | umpire (village matches); kind; questionable eyesight | heroic; white coat, brim hat, dog collar, glasses | 150 Hz soft |\n1085\t| **Lord Rufus Thrumpton-Vane** | villain; out LBW, first ball, on this green on 4 June 1975 and has never forgiven it | bulky; tweed coat, handlebar moustache, monocle hand, flat cap | 160 Hz nasal |\n1086\t| **Sir Aubrey Fennimore-Wolde** | commentator | portrait: grey swept hair, bow tie, panama | 105 Hz |\n1087\t| **Dazza Keegan** | commentator | portrait: sunburnt, zinc cream on nose, cap backwards | 135 Hz |\n1088\t| **Prof. Priya Statsworth** | Owl-Eye analyst | portrait: sharp bob, headset | 210 Hz |\n1089\t\n1090\t### 8.2 Teams (6) and players\n1091\tEach team has 11 players: 3–4 hand-made stars, and the rest generated from the team's name pool and palette. Player stats are 1–10: `bat` (timing), `power`, `tech` (vs pace and spin), `bowl` (type, skill, pace), `field` (`speed`, `catch`, `ground`, `throw`) and `style`.\n1092\t\n1093\t| Team (code) | Kit | Home | Stars (role · special) | Name pool (for generated squad) |\n1094\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1095\t| **Kerfuffle CC** \"The Teapots\" (KER) | cream `#f2ead8`, green trim `#2f6b3a`, green caps | Village Green | Edie Pluckrose (fast bowler, slogger · *Tea-Kettle Slog* / *Vicar's Revenge*), Basil Thwaite (leg-spin · *The Grandad*), Dev Mistry (opener · *Statistical Certainty*), Pip Larkin (keeper · *The Chirp*) | Hodge, Pemberton, Allsop, Twigg, Moss, Fairweather, Hobbs, Nettles |\n1096\t| **Lower Muddleford Mutineers** (MUD) | mud brown `#6a4a2a`, orange `#e07a2a` | Village Green (away) | Gaz Gristle (captain, slogger · *The Long Handle*), Big Terry Dunstable (medium dobber · *Dibbly-Dobbly Doom*), Nan Gristle (wily off-spin) | Clod, Furrow, Bagshaw, Wurzel, Pratt, Muckle |\n1097\t| **Gentlemen of Thrumpton** (GEN) | white, navy `#22305a` stripes, gold `#d8b04a` caps | Thrumpton Hall | Hon. Peregrine Twistleton-Smythe (swing · *The Peregrine Swoop*), Fortescue (butler-fielder, safest hands · *Silver Tray Save*: a guaranteed catch), Lady Araminta Fitch (elegant bat · *The Croquet Drive*) | Ffoulkes, Carstairs, Montague, St John-Smythe, Pargeter |\n1098\t| **Sunburnt Bay Larrikins** (LAR) | teal `#1fb5a8`, yellow `#ffd23a`, zinc stripes | Sunburnt Bay | Shazza Brannigan (express pace · *Sunburn Bouncer*), Kev \"Thongs\" Malone (slogger · *Boardwalk Bludgeon*), Big Wal (keeper) | Dunno, Bluey, Sandy, Robbo, Gazza, Davo |\n1099\t| **Magic Circle XI** \"The Conjurers\" (MAG) | purple `#5a2a7a`, silver, short capes | Dustbowl Downs | The Great Spinaldo (mystery spin · *Vanishing Ball*), Madame Zsa-Zsa Flick (googly bowler · *Sawn in Half*: the stumps split comically for a wicket), Houdini Jnr (keeper · *Lightning Stumping*: wider stumping window) | Presto, Abra, Mystique, Prestidigitate, Sleight |\n1100\t| **Thrumpton's Thunderbolts** (THR) | black, violet `#7a3aff`, gold lightning; ghosts pale `#a8e0ff` | The Megadome | Lord Thrumpton-Vane (captain, bat · *Grudge Drive*; bowls the *Grudge Ball*), the Thrumptonator 3000 (bowling machine · *Triple Threat*), Dr Ebenezer Grimble (ghost bat · *Ectoplasmic Edge*), the Eternal XI of 1882 (ghost fielders that phase) | ghosts: Bartholomew, Silas, Ignatius, Obadiah, Cornelius |\n1101\t\n1102\tBatting orders: stars at 1–5. Bowlers: each team has 4–5 bowlers covering ≥ 2 families.\n1103\t\n1104\t### 8.3 Grounds (5) and the Nets\n1105\t| Ground | Boundary rx×ry | Pitch (bounce/turn/seam/pace) | Outfield | Default time / weather | Ends | Stadium targets (bonus) | Chaos pool |\n1106\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1107\t| **Kerfuffle Village Green** | 560×600, gentle slope (the ball rolls 8% faster down it) | 1.0 / 1.0 / 1.2 / 0.95 | long grass, k ×1.25 | sunny, then golden hour in innings 2 | Pavilion End / Leaning Wicket End | Pub window +6, Vicarage greenhouse +10, Church weathervane +12, Beehive in the oak +4 (bees!) | Doris the cow, bees, church bells (a dot ball rings them) |\n1108\t| **Thrumpton Hall** | 620×620 | 1.0 / 0.9 / 1.1 / 1.0 (swing ×1.5 overcast) | manicured, fast k ×0.8 | overcast | Hall End / Orangery End | Fountain +6 (lost ball), Phantom car windscreen +10, Hall window +8 | peacocks crossing (deflect ground balls), Fortescue's tea tray crossing |\n1109\t| **Sunburnt Bay** | 640×520 (sea side flattened) | 1.25 / 0.9 / 1.0 / 1.15 | sand k ×1.6, running −15% | blazing midday | Pier End / Dunes End | Ferris wheel +12, Ice-cream van +6 (ice-cream rain), Inflatable shark +8 | seagulls steal a stopped ball (2 byes), the tide (sea-side boundary shrinks 15% over the innings), surf spray |\n1110\t| **Dustbowl Downs** | 600×600 | 1.05 / 1.6 / 0.9 / 0.9 (rough patches outside off: turn ×1.5) | bumpy, fast k ×0.85, random small deflections | hot, then a thunderstorm (rain delay in innings 2) | Top Hat End / Water Tower End | Giant top hat +8 (doves), Water tower +10 (brief shower), Hot-air balloon +15 (on a path) | rain delay (Kerfuffle Method), dust devils, rabbits from the hat run across |\n1111\t| **The Thrumpton Megadome** | 760×760 | 1.1 / 1.0 / 1.0 / 1.2 | lightning fast k ×0.7 | midnight, floodlights, fog banks | Jumbotron End / Old Pavilion End | Jumbotron +15, VIP box +12, Ghost bell +12, Laser rig +8 | fog banks, ghost fielders phase (for 0.5 s a ghost can't stop or catch the ball: it passes through), fireworks, Thrumpton's advert break between overs (\"THRUMPTON PARKING: PARK LIKE A LORD\": a 3 s non-interactive card, skippable) |\n1112\t| *Nets* | behind the village pavilion: two netted lanes, the bowling machine, practice stumps | as Village Green | — | day | — | Six Machine targets (6 floating boards) | — |\n1113\t\n1114\t### 8.4 Deliveries\n1115\t#### 8.4.1 Catalogue (speeds nominal km/h; swing + = away from a right-hander; turn in degrees, + = away from a right-hander)\n1116\t| Id | Family | km/h | Swing | Seam | Turn | Bounce | Dip | Notes |\n1117\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1118\t| express | pace | 138–148 | 0.1 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | stock fast ball |\n1119\t| bouncer | pace | 135–145 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.25 | 0 | must pitch ≥ 140 from the batter |\n1120\t| yorker | pace | 136–146 | 0.15 | 0.5 | 0 | 0.9 | 0.1 | length band 0–24 from the crease |\n1121\t| slower | pace | 105–115 | 0 | 1.2 | 0 | 0.95 | 0.3 | looks like an express until late (no speed shown until it pitches) |\n1122\t| outswing | swing | 125–135 | +1.0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | |\n1123\t| inswing | swing | 125–135 | −1.0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | |\n1124\t| wobble | swing | 120–130 | ±0.3 random | 3.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | |\n1125\t| dobber | medium | 100–110 | 0.1 | 1.5 | 0 | 0.95 | 0.1 | |\n1126\t| cutter | medium | 105–115 | 0 | 1.0 | +3 | 0.95 | 0 | |\n1127\t| knuckle | medium | 95–105 | wobbly flight | 0.5 | 0 | 0.9 | 0.25 | |\n1128\t| legbreak | spin | 78–88 | drift −0.3 | 0.3 | +9 | 1.05 | 0.2 | |\n1129\t| googly | spin | 76–86 | drift +0.2 | 0.3 | −8 | 1.05 | 0.2 | |\n1130\t| topspin | spin | 80–90 | 0 | 0.3 | 0 | 1.2 | 0.35 | |\n1131\t| offbreak | spin | 80–90 | drift +0.3 | 0.3 | −8 | 1.0 | 0.15 | |\n1132\t| armball | spin | 88–96 | +0.3 | 0.3 | 0 | 0.95 | 0 | |\n1133\t| doosra | spin | 78–88 | 0 | 0.3 | +8 | 1.05 | 0.2 | |\n1134\t| piston | machine | 160–170 | 0 | 0.8 | 0 | 1.05 | 0 | the Thrumptonator only |\n1135\t| steamBouncer | machine | 150 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.35 | 0 | steam trail |\n1136\t| spinCycle | machine | 95 | 0 | 0 | ±14 random | 1.1 | 0.3 | |\n1137\t\n1138\tSwing base acceleration: 60 u/s² × swing × `T('swing')` × ground factor. Each bowler lists 3 deliveries from their family (plus a special).\n1139\t\n1140\t#### 8.4.2 Field presets (θ° from straight, + = off side; distance in units; the keeper is extra)\n1141\t- **Attacking pace:** slip1 165/150, slip2 158/150, slip3 151/152, gully 132/150, point 95/230, cover 58/260, mid-off 14/300, mid-on −14/300, fine leg −162/(boundary − 30).\n1142\t- **Balanced:** slip1 165/150, point 95/240, cover 55/270, mid-off 12/320, mid-on −12/320, midwicket −60/270, square leg −95/250, fine leg −160/(b − 30), third man 155/(b − 30).\n1143\t- **Defensive:** point 95/250, deep cover 55/(b − 30), long-off 12/(b − 30), long-on −12/(b − 30), deep midwicket −60/(b − 30), deep square −95/(b − 30), fine leg −160/(b − 30), third man 155/(b − 30), cover 40/260.\n1144\t- **Spin attack:** slip 160/40, short leg −100/50, silly point 100/50, cover 55/240, mid-off 12/280, mid-on −12/280, midwicket −60/240, deep square −95/(b − 30), long-on −15/(b − 30). The keeper stands up at 24.\n1145\t\n1146\t### 8.5 Shots (resolver rows; sectors in batter-frame degrees, + off side, 0 straight, ±180 behind)\n1147\t| Button | Length | Sector | Shot | contactAt | Launch | Speed (u/s) | Zone line / z |\n1148\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1149\t| ✕ | full | −25..25 | straight drive | 0.13 | 3° | 440 | −6..8 / 0..14 |\n1150\t| ✕ | full | 25..75 | cover drive | 0.13 | 4° | 450 | −4..14 / 0..14 |\n1151\t| ✕ | full | −75..−25 | on drive | 0.13 | 4° | 430 | −8..6 / 0..14 |\n1152\t| ✕ | full/good | −130..−75 | flick off the pads | 0.12 | 6° | 400 | −10..2 / 0..18 |\n1153\t| ✕ | full/good | −180..−130 | leg glance | 0.11 | 3° | 330 | −10..0 / 0..20 |\n1154\t| ✕ | good | 25..75 | back-foot punch | 0.12 | 5° | 410 | −4..14 / 6..22 |\n1155\t| ✕ | short | −130..−60 | pull | 0.12 | 8° | 460 | −6..10 / 14..32 |\n1156\t| ✕ | short/good (line > 8 off) | 75..125 | square cut | 0.11 | 5° | 460 | 6..22 / 6..26 |\n1157\t| ✕ | any | 125..180 | late cut / dab | 0.10 | 2° | 300 | 4..20 / 2..22 |\n1158\t| ✕ | any | other | push (in that direction) | 0.12 | 3° | 320 | −8..12 / 0..24 |\n1159\t| □ | full | −30..30 | lofted straight hit | 0.14 | 38° | 330 | −6..8 / 0..16 |\n1160\t| □ | full | 30..80 | inside-out lofted cover | 0.14 | 34° | 320 | −2..16 / 0..16 |\n1161\t| □ | full/good | −110..−30 | slog / slog-sweep (vs spin) | 0.15 | 36° | 335 | −10..8 / 0..20 |\n1162\t| □ | short | −140..−60 | hook | 0.12 | 30° | 340 | −6..10 / 18..38 |\n1163\t| □ | short | 60..120 | upper cut | 0.11 | 34° | 310 | 4..20 / 18..36 |\n1164\t| □ | any | 150..180 or −180..−150 | scoop / ramp (over the keeper) | 0.12 | 42° | 260 | −4..6 / 0..20 |\n1165\t| □ | yorker | −30..30 | helicopter (360° follow-through) | 0.12 | 40° | 350 | −4..6 / 0..6 |\n1166\t| ○ | full/good | any | forward defence | 0.08 | 0° | 60 | −8..12 / 0..20 |\n1167\t| ○ | short | any | back defence (duck if z > 28) | 0.08 | 0° | 50 | −8..12 / 8..28 |\n1168\t| none | — | — | leave (duck or sway if z > 28) | — | — | — | — |\n1169\t\n1170\tLengths are measured from the striker's popping crease to where the ball pitched (or would pitch): yorker ≤ 24, full 24–70, good 70–130, short > 130.\n1171\t\n1172\t### 8.6 Specials\n1173\t| Special | Owner | Kind | Effect |\n1174\t|---|---|---|---|\n1175\t| Tea-Kettle Slog | Edie | bat | guaranteed PERFECT lofted hit in the aimed direction, +25% distance, a steam-whistle trail; any delivery |\n1176\t| Vicar's Revenge | Edie | bowl | a 155 km/h inswinging yorker, green meter, holy-light trail; the edge zone ×1.5 vs the batter |\n1177\t| The Grandad | Basil | bowl | a leg-break that bounces three times (each bounce turns +6°) and still reaches the stumps at a crawl; the batter's timing windows halved (the shock) |\n1178\t| Statistical Certainty | Dev | bat | shows the exact perfect timing marker (a ring closing on the bat) for 1 ball; GOOD guaranteed, PERFECT if pressed on the marker |\n1179\t| The Chirp | Pip | field | while bowling: on the next ball a CPU batter's timing error doubles (it gets flustered), or a human batter's timing windows shrink by 30%; costs 50 Hype |\n1180\t| The Long Handle | Gaz (CPU) | bat | a lofted hit with power ×1.4 |\n1181\t| Dibbly-Dobbly Doom | Big Terry (CPU) | bowl | an 80 km/h ball that wobbles in the air; batters mistime it (AI σ ×2) |\n1182\t| Peregrine Swoop | Peregrine | bowl | banana swing ×3, late |\n1183\t| Silver Tray Save | Fortescue | field | the next catch chance is guaranteed (a tray flourish) |\n1184\t| The Croquet Drive | Araminta | bat | a ground shot that can't be stopped (it passes through fielders) and goes for FOUR |\n1185\t| Sunburn Bouncer | Shazza | bowl | a 152 km/h bouncer with heat haze; ducking makes it a dot, a hook without PERFECT gives a top-edge catch |\n1186\t| Boardwalk Bludgeon | Kev | bat | a huge hit, +40% distance, but caught if a fielder is under it |\n1187\t| Vanishing Ball | Spinaldo | bowl | invisible from 40% to 65% of the flight (smoke puffs); the shadow is still drawn (fair) |\n1188\t| Sawn in Half | Zsa-Zsa | bowl | a googly; a bowled wicket splits the stumps |\n1189\t| Lightning Stumping | Houdini Jnr | field | the stumping window triples for 1 over |\n1190\t| Grudge Ball | Thrumpton | bowl | an LBW-seeking yorker; the umpire's accuracy +10% on that ball (a running joke: it doesn't help him) |\n1191\t| Grudge Drive | Thrumpton | bat | a power drive straight at the bowler |\n1192\t| Triple Threat | Thrumptonator | bowl | releases 3 balls: 2 holograms on different lines and lengths, 1 real one (with a seam glint every 0.1 s); only the real one matters |\n1193\t| Ectoplasmic Edge | Grimble | bat | the ball passes through the first fielder it meets |\n1194\t\n1195\t### 8.7 Items, tea treats and chaos\n1196\t#### 8.7.1 Items (Kerfuffle rules)\n1197\t| Item | Side | Effect |\n1198\t|---|---|---|\n1199\t| Golden Teapot | bat | the next scoring shot's runs ×2 (the bonus is shown) |\n1200\t| Lucky Horseshoe | bat | the next dismissal is overturned (\"The ball hits the horseshoe! NOT OUT!\") |\n1201\t| Giant Bat | bat | the bat is drawn 1.6× bigger; zones and windows ×1.4 for 2 balls |\n1202\t| Cake Slice | bat or bowl | Hype +40 |\n1203\t| Sticky Gloves | bowl | the next catch chance is guaranteed |\n1204\t| Banana Peel | bowl | the next run attempt: batters slip mid-pitch (−40% speed for 1 s) |\n1205\t| Fog Machine | bowl | the next ball: the batter's pitch marker is hidden; CPU σ ×1.5 |\n1206\t\n1207\t**Tea treats** (story, at the innings break, pick one): Victoria Sponge (Hype +40), Builder's Tea (timing windows +10% for 2 overs), Cucumber Sandwiches (run speed +10% for the innings).\n1208\t\n1209\t#### 8.7.2 Stadium targets\n1210\tSee §8.3. Each is an entry `{ id, ground, shape: 'box'|'sphere', at, size, bonus, hype: 30, state, fx, line }`.\n1211\t\n1212\t#### 8.7.3 Chaos events\n1213\tEach event is `{ id, ground, when: 'between'|'overStart', chance, duration, run(game, match) generator }`. Each must end by itself and restore the field:\n1214\t- Doris the cow: walks the outfield on a path; fielders path round her; she leaves after 2 overs, or at once if a ball hits her, harmlessly (\"She's taken it on the flank and seems pleased\");\n1215\t- bees from the hive: chase a fielder (−30% speed) for 1 over;\n1216\t- church bells: cosmetic, plus a commentary line;\n1217\t- peacocks: wander and deflect ground balls ±25°;\n1218\t- Fortescue's tea tray: a fielder runs on with tea; play pauses 3 s;\n1219\t- seagulls: a stopped ball in the outfield is carried 30 units (2 byes);"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17695eeb-ca5d-4805-90b6-169496893b17","uuid":"97cfa36a-5d3f-4442-9189-5b00d1065a36","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:21:44.683Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-062125__xe36ddc/work/PLAN.md","content":"| `pavilionClock`, `veranda` | pavilion details | green |\n| `teaUrn`, `teapot`, `cakeStand` | tea-room set (with the store's cakes) | cutscenes |\n| `deckchair` | striped canvas deck chair (3 colourways) | green, hall, bay |\n| `umbrellaOpen` | crowd umbrella (rain) | downs |\n| `covers` | blue tarpaulin over the pitch, rolled or spread (params `spread: 0..1`) | rain delay |\n| `roller` | heavy groundsman's roller | green, cutscene |\n| `floodlight` | lattice pylon with a lamp bank (`lights`) | dome, night matches |\n| `adBoard` | boundary board with a sponsor name painted (params `text`, colours): *Crumb's Cakes*, *Leaning Wicket Ales*, *Thrumpton Holdings*, *Kerfuffle Teas* | all |\n| `pubFront` | the Leaning Wicket's frontage, with a breakable window sprite | green |\n| `greenhouse` | the glass-pane vicarage greenhouse (shatterable) | green |\n| `churchSpire`, `weathervane` | the weathervane spins on hit (`params: { angle }` in 16 steps) | green |\n| `oakTree` | the big oak inside the boundary (a large `tree` variant), with a beehive | green |\n| `fountain` | a tiered fountain with water drawn live | hall |\n| `phantomCar` | Thrumpton's vintage car (original design: long bonnet, running boards) | green, hall |\n| `peacock` | sprite frames: walk and display fan | hall |\n| `beachHut` | striped hut | bay |\n| `pier`, `ferrisWheel` | pier with a Ferris wheel (`params: { angle }` turning) | bay |\n| `iceCreamVan` | van with a giant cone | bay |\n| `inflatableShark` | the shark | bay |\n| `seagull` | sprite frames: flap, glide, carry a ball | bay |\n| `topHat` | giant magician's top hat on the boundary | downs |\n| `waterTower` | a timber water tower: a round tank on four braced stilts, with a ladder | downs |\n| `hotAirBalloon` | drifting on an `E.Path` | downs |\n| `caravan` | magician's caravan | downs |\n| `megadomeTier`, `vipBox`, `laserRig`, `ghostBell` | Megadome set | dome |\n| `thrumptonator` | the steam bowling machine: brass boiler, pipes, a throwing wheel (`params: { angle }`), pressure gauge, smoke from `particles.smoke` | dome, showdown, hub |\n| `minibus` | the Kerfuffle Express (map and cutscene) | map |\n| `cow` | Doris: a Friesian built from parts, with leg-swing animation via params (`step: 0..15`) | green |\n| `coin` | toss coin sprite frames (8) | toss |\n| `itemTokens` | sprites (16×16): Golden Teapot, Lucky Horseshoe, Giant Bat, Cake Slice, Sticky Gloves, Banana Peel, Fog Machine | items |\n\n### 6.6 Effects (`33-fx.js`)\n- **Ball:** a trail (the last 12 positions, fading), a shadow, a speed-streak for >140 km/h, a glow at night.\n- **Bat contact:** splinters (`particles.bits`, willow colours) and an impact star on PERFECT.\n- **Bowled:** stumps knocked back, bails as physics sprites spinning away, a dust burst and a camera shake of 2. With a special: the stumps cartwheel high (over the top) and land in the keeper's hands.\n- **ON FIRE:** flame particles on the bat or ball (`particles.fire`) with an emissive glow.\n- **Specials:**\n  - Tea-Kettle Slog: a steam-whistle trail and steam puffs;\n  - Vicar's Revenge: a holy-light ray and a choir chord;\n  - The Grandad: three dust puffs;\n  - Peregrine Swoop: a feather trail;\n  - Sunburn Bouncer: heat haze (a row-offset shimmer on the overlay);\n  - Vanishing Ball: a puff of purple smoke, gone for 0.3 s, then a puff again;\n  - Triple Threat: two hologram balls (cyan, flickering) and one real one (a seam glint);\n  - Grudge Ball: a red outline;\n  - Ectoplasmic Edge: ghost trails.\n- **Sixes:** the ball lands in the stands with a crowd scatter and a \"crowd catch\" arm. Fireworks on sixes at night (`particles.explosion` small, no shake) and confetti on wins.\n- **Weather:** rain (engine), puddles on the covers, fog overlay, dust devils (`particles.dust` spirals), drifting cloud shadows.\n- **Rule:** all effects respect Comfort settings (reduce motion: no shake, shorter flashes).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Animation (`32-anim.js`)\nBase: the engine's procedural Humanoid. Build cricket-specific motion from four tools:\n- **(a)** `E.Attack` specs with custom `a0/a1/z0/z1/reach/hand:'both'/plane/lunge/crouch/lean/twist/hold`, and phases timed so that \"active\" starts at the shot's `contactAt`;\n- **(b)** poses (`pose`, `expr`, `stance`, `crouch`, `run`, `down`);\n- **(c)** `rig.solvePose` post-processing (wrap it per rig) to place hands with `E.ik3` for two-handed bat grips, the bowling arm's vertical windmill and umpire signals;\n- **(d)** `E.ACTIONS` entries for dives, slides and the run turn (`{ beats, setup, at }`).\n\nCheck every motion with `node engine/tools/filmstrip.mjs dist/index.html#<scene> --steps \"...\" --seed 1`. Each must wind up, strike and settle back without snapping or sweeping backwards.\n\n| Role | Animations |\n|---|---|\n| Batter | stance (side-on, knees flexed, bat tapping), trigger step, front-foot and back-foot defence, leave (bat high), duck and sway, drives (straight, cover, on), cut, pull, hook, flick, glance, sweep, slog-sweep, lofted drive, scoop, upper cut, helicopter (a full wrist whirl: bat rotates 360° after contact), charge (2 quick steps), run carrying the bat, the crease turn (an `E.ACTIONS` pivot with the bat grounded), the dive (body flat, bat stretched: `down` plus a lunge), walk-off (`hunch`, slow), celebrations (bat raised for 50 or a six; a bat twirl), dejection (`kneel`) |\n| Bowler | run-up (pace: accelerating; spin: 4 steps), the bound (a hop), the delivery stride: front arm up, then the bowling arm windmills over the top in the vertical plane, the right hand IK'd round a circle centred on the shoulder (radius = the arm's length) over 0.18 s, with the release at the top front. Then the follow-through (a stoop, then running off to the side of the pitch). A spinner's version is shorter with a wrist flick. Also the appeal (both arms up, `shout`), the aeroplane celebration (arms out, a curved run), a knee slide, hands on head |\n| Fielders | walking in (crouched), the ready position, chase, slide stop, pick-up, overarm throw (wind back, sling: the `throw` move), underarm flick, the diving catch (an `E.ACTIONS` full-length dive and roll), the high catch (hands cupped above the eyes), juggle, drop, the catch celebration (ball tossed up), backing up |\n| Keeper | crouch, rise with the ball, catch (gloves up), dive, stumping (whip the bails: a fast hand arc), standing up to spin |\n| Umpire | stand with hands behind back, slight crouch at delivery. Signals: OUT (finger raised slowly; Rev. Hollis takes 1.2 s), FOUR (arm waved across the chest), SIX (both arms up), WIDE (arms out horizontally), NO BALL (one arm out), BYE (palm up), LEG BYE (touch a raised knee), FREE HIT (circling finger over the head), REVIEW (draws a TV rectangle in the air), DEAD BALL (crossing wrists) |\n| Others | Thrumpton's sneer and monocle-adjust (a hand to the eye), Mrs Crumb pouring tea, Doris grazing and walking, seagulls flap, the peacock's fan display, ghosts float (a z bob plus alpha flicker), the mascot runner in a chicken costume (a hood plus beak colours) chased by two stewards, the crowd |\n\nAnimation tests: filmstrips reviewed (§11.5); and headless checks that every shot's \"active\" phase begins within ±8 ms of its `contactAt`, the bowling hand passes over the head (z > head z) during the stride, and every signal ends back at rest.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Content\n\n### 8.1 Cast (main characters)\n| Name | Role | Look (rig) | Voice |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Edie Pluckrose** | Kerfuffle CC captain; fast bowler and big hitter; the vicar's daughter, unflappable | heroic, size 1.2; auburn ponytail; cream kit, green cap and trim; freckles (portrait detail) | 240 Hz, brisk |\n| **Basil Thwaite** | 74-year-old leg-spinner; claims he once bowled out a duke | chibi, walrus moustache, bald under a faded green cap, cardigan (coat outfit, beige) | 120 Hz wobbly |\n| **Dev Mistry** | opening batter; leaves everything; quotes statistics | heroic; neat black hair; glasses; helmet | 170 Hz precise |\n| **Pip Larkin** | teenage keeper; never stops chirping | chibi; spiky blonde hair; oversized gloves | 290 Hz fast |\n| **Mrs Agatha Crumb** | tea lady, scorer and tactical genius; runs the Nets lessons | chibi; grey bun; floral apron (robe outfit) | 220 Hz warm |\n| **Rev. Hollis** | umpire (village matches); kind; questionable eyesight | heroic; white coat, brim hat, dog collar, glasses | 150 Hz soft |\n| **Lord Rufus Thrumpton-Vane** | villain; out LBW, first ball, on this green on 4 June 1975 and has never forgiven it | bulky; tweed coat, handlebar moustache, monocle hand, flat cap | 160 Hz nasal |\n| **Sir Aubrey Fennimore-Wolde** | commentator | portrait: grey swept hair, bow tie, panama | 105 Hz |\n| **Dazza Keegan** | commentator | portrait: sunburnt, zinc cream on nose, cap backwards | 135 Hz |\n| **Prof. Priya Statsworth** | Owl-Eye analyst | portrait: sharp bob, headset | 210 Hz |\n\n### 8.2 Teams (6) and players\nEach team has 11 players: 3–4 hand-made stars, and the rest generated from the team's name pool and palette. Player stats are 1–10: `bat` (timing), `power`, `tech` (vs pace and spin), `bowl` (type, skill, pace), `field` (`speed`, `catch`, `ground`, `throw`) and `style`.\n\n| Team (code) | Kit | Home | Stars (role · special) | Name pool (for generated squad) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Kerfuffle CC** \"The Teapots\" (KER) | cream `#f2ead8`, green trim `#2f6b3a`, green caps | Village Green | Edie Pluckrose (fast bowler, slogger · *Tea-Kettle Slog* / *Vicar's Revenge*), Basil Thwaite (leg-spin · *The Grandad*), Dev Mistry (opener · *Statistical Certainty*), Pip Larkin (keeper · *The Chirp*) | Hodge, Pemberton, Allsop, Twigg, Moss, Fairweather, Hobbs, Nettles |\n| **Lower Muddleford Mutineers** (MUD) | mud brown `#6a4a2a`, orange `#e07a2a` | Village Green (away) | Gaz Gristle (captain, slogger · *The Long Handle*), Big Terry Dunstable (medium dobber · *Dibbly-Dobbly Doom*), Nan Gristle (wily off-spin) | Clod, Furrow, Bagshaw, Wurzel, Pratt, Muckle |\n| **Gentlemen of Thrumpton** (GEN) | white, navy `#22305a` stripes, gold `#d8b04a` caps | Thrumpton Hall | Hon. Peregrine Twistleton-Smythe (swing · *The Peregrine Swoop*), Fortescue (butler-fielder, safest hands · *Silver Tray Save*: a guaranteed catch), Lady Araminta Fitch (elegant bat · *The Croquet Drive*) | Ffoulkes, Carstairs, Montague, St John-Smythe, Pargeter |\n| **Sunburnt Bay Larrikins** (LAR) | teal `#1fb5a8`, yellow `#ffd23a`, zinc stripes | Sunburnt Bay | Shazza Brannigan (express pace · *Sunburn Bouncer*), Kev \"Thongs\" Malone (slogger · *Boardwalk Bludgeon*), Big Wal (keeper) | Dunno, Bluey, Sandy, Robbo, Gazza, Davo |\n| **Magic Circle XI** \"The Conjurers\" (MAG) | purple `#5a2a7a`, silver, short capes | Dustbowl Downs | The Great Spinaldo (mystery spin · *Vanishing Ball*), Madame Zsa-Zsa Flick (googly bowler · *Sawn in Half*: the stumps split comically for a wicket), Houdini Jnr (keeper · *Lightning Stumping*: wider stumping window) | Presto, Abra, Mystique, Prestidigitate, Sleight |\n| **Thrumpton's Thunderbolts** (THR) | black, violet `#7a3aff`, gold lightning; ghosts pale `#a8e0ff` | The Megadome | Lord Thrumpton-Vane (captain, bat · *Grudge Drive*; bowls the *Grudge Ball*), the Thrumptonator 3000 (bowling machine · *Triple Threat*), Dr Ebenezer Grimble (ghost bat · *Ectoplasmic Edge*), the Eternal XI of 1882 (ghost fielders that phase) | ghosts: Bartholomew, Silas, Ignatius, Obadiah, Cornelius |\n\nBatting orders: stars at 1–5. Bowlers: each team has 4–5 bowlers covering ≥ 2 families.\n\n### 8.3 Grounds (5) and the Nets\n| Ground | Boundary rx×ry | Pitch (bounce/turn/seam/pace) | Outfield | Default time / weather | Ends | Stadium targets (bonus) | Chaos pool |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Kerfuffle Village Green** | 560×600, gentle slope (the ball rolls 8% faster down it) | 1.0 / 1.0 / 1.2 / 0.95 | long grass, k ×1.25 | sunny, then golden hour in innings 2 | Pavilion End / Leaning Wicket End | Pub window +6, Vicarage greenhouse +10, Church weathervane +12, Beehive in the oak +4 (bees!) | Doris the cow, bees, church bells (a dot ball rings them) |\n| **Thrumpton Hall** | 620×620 | 1.0 / 0.9 / 1.1 / 1.0 (swing ×1.5 overcast) | manicured, fast k ×0.8 | overcast | Hall End / Orangery End | Fountain +6 (lost ball), Phantom car windscreen +10, Hall window +8 | peacocks crossing (deflect ground balls), Fortescue's tea tray crossing |\n| **Sunburnt Bay** | 640×520 (sea side flattened) | 1.25 / 0.9 / 1.0 / 1.15 | sand k ×1.6, running −15% | blazing midday | Pier End / Dunes End | Ferris wheel +12, Ice-cream van +6 (ice-cream rain), Inflatable shark +8 | seagulls steal a stopped ball (2 byes), the tide (sea-side boundary shrinks 15% over the innings), surf spray |\n| **Dustbowl Downs** | 600×600 | 1.05 / 1.6 / 0.9 / 0.9 (rough patches outside off: turn ×1.5) | bumpy, fast k ×0.85, random small deflections | hot, then a thunderstorm (rain delay in innings 2) | Top Hat End / Water Tower End | Giant top hat +8 (doves), Water tower +10 (brief shower), Hot-air balloon +15 (on a path) | rain delay (Kerfuffle Method), dust devils, rabbits from the hat run across |\n| **The Thrumpton Megadome** | 760×760 | 1.1 / 1.0 / 1.0 / 1.2 | lightning fast k ×0.7 | midnight, floodlights, fog banks | Jumbotron End / Old Pavilion End | Jumbotron +15, VIP box +12, Ghost bell +12, Laser rig +8 | fog banks, ghost fielders phase (for 0.5 s a ghost can't stop or catch the ball: it passes through), fireworks, Thrumpton's advert break between overs (\"THRUMPTON PARKING: PARK LIKE A LORD\": a 3 s non-interactive card, skippable) |\n| *Nets* | behind the village pavilion: two netted lanes, the bowling machine, practice stumps | as Village Green | — | day | — | Six Machine targets (6 floating boards) | — |\n\n### 8.4 Deliveries\n#### 8.4.1 Catalogue (speeds nominal km/h; swing + = away from a right-hander; turn in degrees, + = away from a right-hander)\n| Id | Family | km/h | Swing | Seam | Turn | Bounce | Dip | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| express | pace | 138–148 | 0.1 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | stock fast ball |\n| bouncer | pace | 135–145 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.25 | 0 | must pitch ≥ 140 from the batter |\n| yorker | pace | 136–146 | 0.15 | 0.5 | 0 | 0.9 | 0.1 | length band 0–24 from the crease |\n| slower | pace | 105–115 | 0 | 1.2 | 0 | 0.95 | 0.3 | looks like an express until late (no speed shown until it pitches) |\n| outswing | swing | 125–135 | +1.0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | |\n| inswing | swing | 125–135 | −1.0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | |\n| wobble | swing | 120–130 | ±0.3 random | 3.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | |\n| dobber | medium | 100–110 | 0.1 | 1.5 | 0 | 0.95 | 0.1 | |\n| cutter | medium | 105–115 | 0 | 1.0 | +3 | 0.95 | 0 | |\n| knuckle | medium | 95–105 | wobbly flight | 0.5 | 0 | 0.9 | 0.25 | |\n| legbreak | spin | 78–88 | drift −0.3 | 0.3 | +9 | 1.05 | 0.2 | |\n| googly | spin | 76–86 | drift +0.2 | 0.3 | −8 | 1.05 | 0.2 | |\n| topspin | spin | 80–90 | 0 | 0.3 | 0 | 1.2 | 0.35 | |\n| offbreak | spin | 80–90 | drift +0.3 | 0.3 | −8 | 1.0 | 0.15 | |\n| armball | spin | 88–96 | +0.3 | 0.3 | 0 | 0.95 | 0 | |\n| doosra | spin | 78–88 | 0 | 0.3 | +8 | 1.05 | 0.2 | |\n| piston | machine | 160–170 | 0 | 0.8 | 0 | 1.05 | 0 | the Thrumptonator only |\n| steamBouncer | machine | 150 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.35 | 0 | steam trail |\n| spinCycle | machine | 95 | 0 | 0 | ±14 random | 1.1 | 0.3 | |\n\nSwing base acceleration: 60 u/s² × swing × `T('swing')` × ground factor. Each bowler lists 3 deliveries from their family (plus a special).\n\n#### 8.4.2 Field presets (θ° from straight, + = off side; distance in units; the keeper is extra)\n- **Attacking pace:** slip1 165/150, slip2 158/150, slip3 151/152, gully 132/150, point 95/230, cover 58/260, mid-off 14/300, mid-on −14/300, fine leg −162/(boundary − 30).\n- **Balanced:** slip1 165/150, point 95/240, cover 55/270, mid-off 12/320, mid-on −12/320, midwicket −60/270, square leg −95/250, fine leg −160/(b − 30), third man 155/(b − 30).\n- **Defensive:** point 95/250, deep cover 55/(b − 30), long-off 12/(b − 30), long-on −12/(b − 30), deep midwicket −60/(b − 30), deep square −95/(b − 30), fine leg −160/(b − 30), third man 155/(b − 30), cover 40/260.\n- **Spin attack:** slip 160/40, short leg −100/50, silly point 100/50, cover 55/240, mid-off 12/280, mid-on −12/280, midwicket −60/240, deep square −95/(b − 30), long-on −15/(b − 30). The keeper stands up at 24.\n\n### 8.5 Shots (resolver rows; sectors in batter-frame degrees, + off side, 0 straight, ±180 behind)\n| Button | Length | Sector | Shot | contactAt | Launch | Speed (u/s) | Zone line / z |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| ✕ | full | −25..25 | straight drive | 0.13 | 3° | 440 | −6..8 / 0..14 |\n| ✕ | full | 25..75 | cover drive | 0.13 | 4° | 450 | −4..14 / 0..14 |\n| ✕ | full | −75..−25 | on drive | 0.13 | 4° | 430 | −8..6 / 0..14 |\n| ✕ | full/good | −130..−75 | flick off the pads | 0.12 | 6° | 400 | −10..2 / 0..18 |\n| ✕ | full/good | −180..−130 | leg glance | 0.11 | 3° | 330 | −10..0 / 0..20 |\n| ✕ | good | 25..75 | back-foot punch | 0.12 | 5° | 410 | −4..14 / 6..22 |\n| ✕ | short | −130..−60 | pull | 0.12 | 8° | 460 | −6..10 / 14..32 |\n| ✕ | short/good (line > 8 off) | 75..125 | square cut | 0.11 | 5° | 460 | 6..22 / 6..26 |\n| ✕ | any | 125..180 | late cut / dab | 0.10 | 2° | 300 | 4..20 / 2..22 |\n| ✕ | any | other | push (in that direction) | 0.12 | 3° | 320 | −8..12 / 0..24 |\n| □ | full | −30..30 | lofted straight hit | 0.14 | 38° | 330 | −6..8 / 0..16 |\n| □ | full | 30..80 | inside-out lofted cover | 0.14 | 34° | 320 | −2..16 / 0..16 |\n| □ | full/good | −110..−30 | slog / slog-sweep (vs spin) | 0.15 | 36° | 335 | −10..8 / 0..20 |\n| □ | short | −140..−60 | hook | 0.12 | 30° | 340 | −6..10 / 18..38 |\n| □ | short | 60..120 | upper cut | 0.11 | 34° | 310 | 4..20 / 18..36 |\n| □ | any | 150..180 or −180..−150 | scoop / ramp (over the keeper) | 0.12 | 42° | 260 | −4..6 / 0..20 |\n| □ | yorker | −30..30 | helicopter (360° follow-through) | 0.12 | 40° | 350 | −4..6 / 0..6 |\n| ○ | full/good | any | forward defence | 0.08 | 0° | 60 | −8..12 / 0..20 |\n| ○ | short | any | back defence (duck if z > 28) | 0.08 | 0° | 50 | −8..12 / 8..28 |\n| none | — | — | leave (duck or sway if z > 28) | — | — | — | — |\n\nLengths are measured from the striker's popping crease to where the ball pitched (or would pitch): yorker ≤ 24, full 24–70, good 70–130, short > 130.\n\n### 8.6 Specials\n| Special | Owner | Kind | Effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Tea-Kettle Slog | Edie | bat | guaranteed PERFECT lofted hit in the aimed direction, +25% distance, a steam-whistle trail; any delivery |\n| Vicar's Revenge | Edie | bowl | a 155 km/h inswinging yorker, green meter, holy-light trail; the edge zone ×1.5 vs the batter |\n| The Grandad | Basil | bowl | a leg-break that bounces three times (each bounce turns +6°) and still reaches the stumps at a crawl; the batter's timing windows halved (the shock) |\n| Statistical Certainty | Dev | bat | shows the exact perfect timing marker (a ring closing on the bat) for 1 ball; GOOD guaranteed, PERFECT if pressed on the marker |\n| The Chirp | Pip | field | while bowling: on the next ball a CPU batter's timing error doubles (it gets flustered), or a human batter's timing windows shrink by 30%; costs 50 Hype |\n| The Long Handle | Gaz (CPU) | bat | a lofted hit with power ×1.4 |\n| Dibbly-Dobbly Doom | Big Terry (CPU) | bowl | an 80 km/h ball that wobbles in the air; batters mistime it (AI σ ×2) |\n| Peregrine Swoop | Peregrine | bowl | banana swing ×3, late |\n| Silver Tray Save | Fortescue | field | the next catch chance is guaranteed (a tray flourish) |\n| The Croquet Drive | Araminta | bat | a ground shot that can't be stopped (it passes through fielders) and goes for FOUR |\n| Sunburn Bouncer | Shazza | bowl | a 152 km/h bouncer with heat haze; ducking makes it a dot, a hook without PERFECT gives a top-edge catch |\n| Boardwalk Bludgeon | Kev | bat | a huge hit, +40% distance, but caught if a fielder is under it |\n| Vanishing Ball | Spinaldo | bowl | invisible from 40% to 65% of the flight (smoke puffs); the shadow is still drawn (fair) |\n| Sawn in Half | Zsa-Zsa | bowl | a googly; a bowled wicket splits the stumps |\n| Lightning Stumping | Houdini Jnr | field | the stumping window triples for 1 over |\n| Grudge Ball | Thrumpton | bowl | an LBW-seeking yorker; the umpire's accuracy +10% on that ball (a running joke: it doesn't help him) |\n| Grudge Drive | Thrumpton | bat | a power drive straight at the bowler |\n| Triple Threat | Thrumptonator | bowl | releases 3 balls: 2 holograms on different lines and lengths, 1 real one (with a seam glint every 0.1 s); only the real one matters |\n| Ectoplasmic Edge | Grimble | bat | the ball passes through the first fielder it meets |\n\n### 8.7 Items, tea treats and chaos\n#### 8.7.1 Items (Kerfuffle rules)\n| Item | Side | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| Golden Teapot | bat | the next scoring shot's runs ×2 (the bonus is shown) |\n| Lucky Horseshoe | bat | the next dismissal is overturned (\"The ball hits the horseshoe! NOT OUT!\") |\n| Giant Bat | bat | the bat is drawn 1.6× bigger; zones and windows ×1.4 for 2 balls |\n| Cake Slice | bat or bowl | Hype +40 |\n| Sticky Gloves | bowl | the next catch chance is guaranteed |\n| Banana Peel | bowl | the next run attempt: batters slip mid-pitch (−40% speed for 1 s) |\n| Fog Machine | bowl | the next ball: the batter's pitch marker is hidden; CPU σ ×1.5 |\n\n**Tea treats** (story, at the innings break, pick one): Victoria Sponge (Hype +40), Builder's Tea (timing windows +10% for 2 overs), Cucumber Sandwiches (run speed +10% for the innings).\n\n#### 8.7.2 Stadium targets\nSee §8.3. Each is an entry `{ id, ground, shape: 'box'|'sphere', at, size, bonus, hype: 30, state, fx, line }`.\n\n#### 8.7.3 Chaos events\nEach event is `{ id, ground, when: 'between'|'overStart', chance, duration, run(game, match) generator }`. Each must end by itself and restore the field:\n- Doris the cow: walks the outfield on a path; fielders path round her; she leaves after 2 overs, or at once if a ball hits her, harmlessly (\"She's taken it on the flank and seems pleased\");\n- bees from the hive: chase a fielder (−30% speed) for 1 over;\n- church bells: cosmetic, plus a commentary line;\n- peacocks: wander and deflect ground balls ±25°;\n- Fortescue's tea tray: a fielder runs on with tea; play pauses 3 s;\n- seagulls: a stopped ball in the outfield is carried 30 units (2 byes);","numLines":220,"startLine":1000,"totalLines":1435}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Dnur6NE8txUsVaL41S2Yc9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghxXGoVpX2fjf8AHmny3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016LmrcVMJFN7GU4pJJ6drJU","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-062125__xe36ddc/work/PLAN.md","offset":1220,"limit":220},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11633,"cache_read_input_tokens":67819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11633},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17695eeb-ca5d-4805-90b6-169496893b17","uuid":"87b0b3e5-ea65-457e-a11d-4805e71a19ed","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:21:47.652Z","request_id":"req_011CghxXGYctV3e2P3jfovj8","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016LmrcVMJFN7GU4pJJ6drJU":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-062125__xe36ddc/work/PLAN.md","offset":1220,"limit":220}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016LmrcVMJFN7GU4pJJ6drJU","type":"tool_result","content":"1220\t- the tide: the sea-side boundary moves in a step at each over's start (the ellipse's sea-side radius shrinks, up to 15% over the innings). **Don't re-bake the floor for it.** Draw the advancing water edge and the moved rope as animated `r.decal` bands over the baked sand, and tag wet sand logically (a y threshold) for the slower outfield;\n1221\t- the rain delay (scripted in chapter 4; available in Quick Match weather \"rain\"): rain, covers, tea scene, the Kerfuffle Method;\n1222\t- dust devils: deflect aerial balls passing through ±10°;\n1223\t- rabbits: cosmetic;\n1224\t- fog banks: change the fog density over 2 overs;\n1225\t- ghost phasing: a ghost fielder is intangible for 0.5 s at random;\n1226\t- fireworks: on sixes at night;\n1227\t- the advert break: a 3 s card between overs at the Megadome;\n1228\t- the mascot pitch invader: a chicken costume, chased by stewards; cosmetic, 1 over, any ground in Quick Match with Kerfuffle rules.\n1229\t\n1230\t### 8.8 Story: *The Grand Kerfuffle* (5 chapters)\n1231\tThe writing style is dry, affectionate and digressive, like the commentary box; short lines; no line over 2 × 42 characters; markup for comic timing (`{w=.5}`, `{shake}`).\n1232\t\n1233\t**Prologue** (cutscene on the village green at dawn, after New Game):\n1234\t- AUBREY (narrating, as *The Kerfuffle Almanack*): \"Kerfuffle-on-the-Wold. Population: two hundred and twelve, and a cow called Doris.\"\n1235\t- AUBREY: \"Nothing of note has happened here since the hailstorm of 1953,{w=.4} which was rained off.\"\n1236\t- *The Phantom crunches across the square. Tyre marks on the pitch. Mrs Crumb drops a scone.*\n1237\t- THRUMPTON: \"Fourth of June, 1975. First ball. Given out leg before by a vicar{w=.3} who was looking at a butterfly.\"\n1238\t- EDIE: \"That was my grandfather. He still talks about that butterfly.\"\n1239\t- THRUMPTON: \"I have purchased the deeds to this green. On Monday it becomes the Thrumpton Parking Plaza.{w=.3} Four hundred spaces.{w=.3} No cricket.\"\n1240\t- MRS CRUMB: \"Over my dead sponge.\"\n1241\t- THRUMPTON: \"Unless... you beat my teams in the Grand Kerfuffle. Five matches. My grounds. My rules.{w=.3} Your umpires. I'm not a monster.\"\n1242\t- EDIE: \"Done. We'll play you anywhere.{w=.3} Bring cake.\"\n1243\t- *Title card: THE GRAND KERFUFFLE.*\n1244\t\n1245\t| # | Chapter | Opponent · ground | Scenario | Teaches | Beats | Kerfuffle Goals (stars) |\n1246\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1247\t| 1 | **A Gentle Knock** | Lower Muddleford · Village Green | full match, 2 overs each, KER bats first, at the player's difficulty (Muddleford are the weakest side, so it plays gently) | Nets lessons 1–4 and 6: aim, ground, loft, defend, run, bowl | pre: Gaz's challenge (\"by warm-up I mean a thrashing\"); Nets with Mrs Crumb (\"Watch the ball, dear, not the cake\"); after innings 1: Thrumpton watches from the car (\"With the heater on\"); win: \"Beginner's luck. Thrumpton Hall next. Dress code: impeccable.\" | win · smash the pub window · hit a six |\n1248\t| 2 | **Tea on the Lawn** | Gentlemen of Thrumpton · Thrumpton Hall (overcast) | \"Kerfuffle posted 24 after a top-order collapse, chiefly due to peacocks.\" The Gentlemen need 25 from 2 overs: **you bowl and field** | lessons 7–11: aftertouch, Hype specials, catch ring, throws, reviews (the KRS appears) | pre: Peregrine (\"Do mind the peacocks; they bite\"); Fortescue announces tea \"at the fall of the third wicket, or at four, whichever is more dignified\"; mid: the ball comes back sticky (\"Is that... marmalade?\"), a review tutorial; win: \"I shall have Fortescue polish your trophy. With marmalade.\" | win · take a PERFECT-ring catch · win a review |\n1249\t| 3 | **Sand in the Sandwiches** | Sunburnt Bay Larrikins · Sunburnt Bay | chase 30 from 2 overs vs pace: **you bat** | bouncers (duck, hook), hard running and the dive, the tide | pre: the minibus breaks down and the team pushes it (\"Statistically, sunscreen doesn't melt at—\" / \"Mate.\"); mid: the tide warning; win: Shazza warns \"He's been buying ringers. Weird ones. See-through ones.\" | win · hook a six · win with a dive making the crease |\n1250\t| 4 | **Now You See It** | Magic Circle XI · Dustbowl Downs | full match, 2 overs each; a rain delay in innings 2, the Kerfuffle Method | spin (lesson 5: charge), stumpings, the rain delay, tea treats | pre: Spinaldo (\"Pick a card. It will be the card of your downfall.\"), Basil (\"I bowled leg-spin to a magician once. He sawed my stumps in half.\"); mid: rain, covers, the tea room scene, Mrs Crumb's chalkboard (\"carry the scone...\"); win: Spinaldo reveals the ghosts and the midnight booking | win · stump a batter · hit the hot-air balloon |\n1251\t| 5 | **The Midnight Final** | Thrumpton's Thunderbolts · The Megadome (night, fog) | full match, 3 overs each; the final over of the KER chase is the Thrumptonator's boss over; a Super Over if tied | ON FIRE emphasis, Triple Threat, ghosts, fog, the Super Over | pre: the Megadome (\"No tea. No cake. No interval. Just ADVERTS.\"); the ghosts rise (\"We have waited one hundred and forty-four years for a match that wasn't rained off.\" / EDIE: \"Then let's give you one.\"); mid: fog rolls in; the Thrumptonator wheeled out (\"Steam-powered. Never misses. Never gives anyone out leg before on a butterfly.\"); **win ending:** Thrumpton demands one exhibition ball against Rev. Hollis, who gives him out LBW first ball, again. Thrumpton laughs for the first time in 51 years: \"Plumb. Absolutely plumb.\" He tears up the deeds, the ghosts depart in peace (\"Worth the wait.\"), and the Almanack closes: \"Lord Thrumpton-Vane now polishes the tea urn on Saturdays and is said to be adequate at fine leg.\" Then credits. | win · survive the Thrumptonator's over without losing a wicket · hit the jumbotron |\n1252\t\n1253\t**Losses** (every chapter): a short consolation, e.g. MRS CRUMB: \"Never mind, dear. Even the best of us get a golden duck. Have a scone and go again.\" Then Retry / Retry on Village / Map.\n1254\t\n1255\tThe beats run as `game.script` generators on the bus (for example, `yield E.until(() => match.innings === 1 && match.phase === 'between')`, then play the scene). Story scene data goes through `E.Story` nodes, with speakers mapped to portraits.\n1256\t\n1257\t### 8.9 Lines\n1258\t#### 8.9.1 Commentary starter set (write ≥ 3 per event per commentator in this voice; A = Aubrey, D = Dazza)\n1259\t- **match start:** A \"Good afternoon from {ground}, where the sun is out, the tea is stewed, and {team} are about to play cricket, after a fashion.\" D \"Should be a cracker. Or a shambles. Probably both.\"\n1260\t- **dot:** A \"Defended. A stroke of great dignity and no ambition whatsoever.\" D \"Nothing doing.\" A \"Left alone. The ball goes by like a gossip past a closed door.\"\n1261\t- **beaten:** A \"Beaten all ends up! He could not have missed that more if he'd brought a map.\" D \"Played and missed. Dreadful. Lovely ball, mind.\"\n1262\t- **single:** D \"Tip and run.\" A \"A quick single, taken with all the urgency of a vicar late for a fête.\"\n1263\t- **four:** A \"FOUR! Struck with the elegance of a swan, and the violence of an angry swan.\" D \"Too short, too wide, too bad. Four.\"\n1264\t- **six:** A \"That is MAXIMUM! Somebody alert the air-traffic people.\" D \"That's gone into the next postcode, mate.\"\n1265\t- **six into the pub:** A \"Through the window of the Leaning Wicket! Last orders, I fear, have been called by the ball.\"\n1266\t- **greenhouse:** A \"Into the vicarage greenhouse. There goes the marrow competition.\"\n1267\t- **bowled:** A \"Bowled him! The stumps are doing cartwheels, which is more than the batsman managed.\" D \"Timber!\"\n1268\t- **caught:** D \"Up, up... and taken. Safe as houses.\" A \"A catch of quiet magnificence. Someone get that fielder a scone.\"\n1269\t- **dropped:** A \"Dropped! Butter, I think, would have had a firmer grip.\" D \"Oh, he'll be buying the drinks tonight.\"\n1270\t- **LBW:** A \"A huge appeal! The Reverend raises... raises... yes, eventually, the finger.\" D \"Plumb. Plumber than a plumber.\"\n1271\t- **run out:** A \"Yes! No! Wait! Sorry! The four stages of grief, conducted at a sprint.\" D \"Run out by a country mile.\"\n1272\t- **stumped:** A \"Down the pitch, through the gate, and the bails are off before you can say Kerfuffle.\"\n1273\t- **wide:** D \"Wide. Wide enough to land a plane.\"\n1274\t- **no-ball:** A \"No-ball! He's overstepped, which in this village is practically a felony. Free hit to come.\"\n1275\t- **ON FIRE:** D \"The bat is literally smoking. Someone fetch a bucket.\" A \"Willow ablaze! Health and Safety will want a word.\"\n1276\t- **special:** A \"Oh, he's going for something special. I can't look. I'm looking.\"\n1277\t- **review:** PRIYA \"Owl-Eye has it... pitching in line... hitting... and it's clipping the bails by a whisker of a whisker.\"\n1278\t- **rain:** A \"And down it comes. The covers are on, the umbrellas are up, and the crowd are discussing the weather, which is the only thing they love more than cricket.\"\n1279\t- **the cow:** A \"There's a cow on the outfield. A Friesian, I believe. She's at deep midwicket and, frankly, better positioned than their fine leg.\"\n1280\t- **idle filler:** A \"A Mrs Hepplewhite of Lower Muddleford has sent in a lemon drizzle. Mrs Hepplewhite, you are a saint.\" A \"There's a pigeon at short leg who has, I think, been there since Tuesday.\" D \"Lovely day for it.\" A \"Is it? I hadn't noticed. I've been looking at this cake.\"\n1281\t- **win:** A \"And that's the match! Victory for {winner}, for common sense, and for the scone.\" **loss:** D \"That's that, then. Shake hands, have a sandwich, try again.\"\n1282\t\n1283\t#### 8.9.2 Shouts (gibberish voice, captions in speech bubbles)\n1284\t\"YES!\", \"NO!\", \"WAIT!\", \"TWO!\", \"HOWZAT!\", \"OUT!\", \"CATCH IT!\", \"MINE!\", \"SORRY!\", and the crowd's \"KER-FUF-FLE!\".\n1285\t\n1286\t#### 8.9.3 Match report templates (results screen; fill from the ball records; pick by the shape of the result)\n1287\t- \"{winner}, set {target}, were indebted to {topBat} ({topRuns}{notOut}, {sixes} sixes, one of them through {targetHit}). Play was held up for {delayMins} minutes while {chaosThing} was persuaded off the square.\"\n1288\t- \"{loser} never recovered from {collapse}. {topBowl} took {wkts} for {runs} with a mixture of guile, swing and, in one instance, marmalade.\"\n1289\t- \"A tie, decided by a Super Over of almost unbearable tension, at the end of which {hero} was carried from the field on the shoulders of the scorer.\"\n1290\t\n1291\t### 8.10 Music\n1292\tSee §5.13.4. Sketch each song in the notation and audition it in the Nets (a dev-mode \"Jukebox\" row on the JUMP tab plays each song and sting).\n1293\t\n1294\t---\n1295\t\n1296\t## 9. Build order and milestones\n1297\tEach milestone ends with its tests green (`node test/run.mjs`), a bundle build, and a look at the screenshots it touched. Commit nothing outside `<dev>` except the final .html and the exit interview.\n1298\t\n1299\t| M | Name | Builds | Exit criteria |\n1300\t|---|---|---|---|\n1301\t| **M0** | Scaffold | the dev folder; the engine copied; vendor hub files; `tools/build.mjs` producing `dist/` and the single-file bundle with the client first; `test/run.mjs` running a first suite plus the bundle checks; `tools/serve.mjs`; a first title scene with the logo (finished in M4) | `node test/run.mjs` prints `N passed, 0 failed`; the bundle opens from file:// to the title; `engine/tools/check.mjs` passes on the bundle |\n1302\t| **M1** | **The Nets spike (feel first)** | the Village Green TileMap (basic floor texture), the broadcast and wide views; the batter rig with the **bat** (engine change 1) and pads; the bowling machine; the ball physics and predictor; the timing model and ground, loft and block shots for 6 resolver rows; the shadow, pitch marker and timing words; the cut to the wide cam; boundary detection (4 and 6); the TUNING registry and a minimal dev panel (sliders only) | unit-ball and unit-shots green; filmstrips of 3 shots and the bowling machine look right; a human can hit PERFECT drives reliably after 10 balls on County (play it) |\n1303\t| **M2** | Match loop | rules (§5.7), the delivery director, running (§5.4) with the AI partner, fielding (§5.5) for the CPU side, umpire decisions and signals (bowled, caught, LBW, run out, stumped), innings, target, result, toss, Super Over; the CPU batting and bowling AI; Quick Match 1P vs CPU with the human batting and the CPU bowling | unit-rules and unit-umpire green; sim scenarios for running, wickets and boundaries green; **bot-match** (CPU vs CPU, Village Green) completes with a result and no stuck balls |\n1304\t| **M3** | Human bowling and fielding, and the hub early | §5.2 in full (panel, marker, meter, aftertouch, over/round, field presets), catch ring, throws, keeper, bowler select, captain AI; **AI Hub parallel Super Over** (§5.17) with our card | sim scenarios for bowling, catching and throws green; **hub-mock** green; **browser-hub** passes with 1, 2 and 4 players (latency and loss); a full 1P Quick Match playable in both roles |\n1305\t| **M4** | Presentation | the camera director (all shots) and the close and review views; the recorder, replays, Owl-Eye, the third umpire and KRS; the HUD (§5.15.2); glyph prompts (§5.14.3, engine change 4); front-end menus, setup and pause items; settings; the 10-foot layout; the touch-only gate; commentary with captions; the gibberish voice synth (engine change 3); SFX, the crowd engine, music with layers | prompt and glyph tests green; HUD layout tests green on 4 sizes; browser smoke screenshots reviewed; commentary tests green |\n1306\t| **M5** | The arcade layer | Hype, ON FIRE, every special (§8.6), items, tea treats, stadium targets, chaos events, weather and time of day (fog, night lights), difficulty levels | sim scenarios for each special, item, target and chaos event green (forced via debug) |\n1307\t| **M6** | Content | all 5 grounds with their art (§6.3, §6.5), panoramas, props and palettes; the 6 teams and 66 players with rigs, portraits and voices; the story map, the 5 chapters, cutscenes, beats, goals and stars, the endings; the Nets lessons and Six Machine; Showdown Bat and Bowl with tables; Versus with 2–4 players; saves, unlocks; Wisden-style reports; all music | **bot-campaign** completes the story; bot-match on all grounds; local MP tests green; screenshots of every ground and kit reviewed |\n1308\t| **M7** | Attract, dev, about, polish | the attract showreel (10 segments) and its coverage; the full dev panel (4 tabs, every toggle and action); About/Credits pages; engine changes logged; balance passes with the dev sliders (aim: a County CPU chase of 30 off 2 overs succeeds about 50% vs a competent human); final bundle; exit-interview.json | **all suites green**, including attract-coverage, dev, bundle and the browser hub runs; no TODO or FIXME strings in `src/` (a test greps for them); the final reply written |\n1309\t\n1310\tWork inside each milestone in this order: simulation (with unit tests), then presentation, then scenario tests, then screenshots.\n1311\t\n1312\t---\n1313\t\n1314\t## 10. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1315\t\n1316\t| # | Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk now | Complete fallback if it fails |\n1317\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1318\t| 1 | **Batting feel and readability** in an orthographic view | the depth and height of a fast ball are ambiguous without perspective; batting is the game | M1 first: the shadow disc, the pitch marker, the trail and length bands; the timing words; tune `camPitch`, `camScale`, `ballSpeed` and the windows with dev sliders; human playtest after M1 | raise the pitch marker to always-on with a closing timing ring (Statistical Certainty's visual) as the default \"Classic\" assist |\n1319\t| 2 | **Bat and two-handed shots on the rig** | the engine rig has swords, not bats; two-handed IK in the draw pose could fight the attack specs | engine change 1 in M1 plus a filmstrip of each shot family; put the left hand on the handle by IK *after* the attack pose; keep `hand: 'both'` specs | a one-handed bat hold (the left hand following loosely), which still reads as a bat at 40 px |\n1320\t| 3 | **Bowling action (windmill)** | there's no stock move for a vertical overarm arc | `solvePose` post-processing with an `E.ik3` circle over 0.18 s; filmstrip; compare with the `throw` move | the engine's `throw` move with a higher `z1` and a hop, which reads as overarm |\n1321\t| 4 | **Physics, predictor and AI coherence** | the AI, LBW, catches and Owl-Eye all depend on the predictor matching reality | one step function shared by the sim and the predictor; no randomness inside it (the seam deviation is stored at release); unit test the match within 0.01 units | the AI and fielders read a simpler ballistic prediction, and LBW and Owl-Eye use the recorded real path up to impact plus a ballistic continuation from it |\n1322\t| 5 | **Floor baking with big grounds and several views** | each view and scale bakes the floor; the cache clears past 6; zoom tweens re-bake | fixed views (no zoom tweens), raise the limit to 10 (engine change 6), warm the bakes in boot, chunked bakes; instrument `map.floors` | smaller grounds (rx 520) and only 3 views (close becomes broadcast with a tighter focus) |\n1323\t| 6 | **Stalled deliveries** (a fielder never reaches the ball, a ball never settles) | a stuck game is game-breaking | a timeout on every director state; the 15 s inPlay cap; the bot-match stuck check | already complete: the timeouts are the fallback |\n1324\t| 7 | **AI Hub conformance** | the client must come first; no blur pause; ready with no key; Enter on our card; time-up and end handling | M3 early; harness runs in the test command; `autoPause: false` in sessions; `card: true` handled with keys, pad and clicks | use the hub's own card (`card: false`), which removes the Enter check |\n1325\t| 8 | **Content volume** (5 grounds, 6 teams, story, lines) | it can crowd out polish | data registries plus the ground recipe builder; a squad generator; stars hand-made only; content in M6 after systems are final | fewer props per ground and shorter line pools (≥ 3 per event), never fewer grounds or chapters |\n1326\t| 9 | **Gibberish voice quality and clipping** | many simultaneous syllables could clip or sound harsh | a voice bus with a compressor (`DynamicsCompressorNode`); max 2 voices at once (queue); audition in the dev Jukebox | simpler square-blip voices with per-speaker pitch, still gibberish |\n1327\t| 10 | **The attract mode looping forever without errors** | long unattended runs find rare bugs | it uses the real machinery with cheats; the attract-coverage test runs 12 minutes; `game.errors` stays empty | fewer segments (keep ≥ 6, covering the coverage list) |\n1328\t| 11 | **Input conflicts** (J/K/L confirm and cancel, hub Create + Options, rebinding) | wrong menu behaviour annoys at once | a custom preset with confirm J and cancel L; engine change 5; tests for prompts and rebinding | — |\n1329\t| 12 | **Bundle size or an inline `</script>`** | a broken single file is a broken deliverable | the build escapes it, then a bundle test opens the bundle headless and in a browser | — |\n1330\t\n1331\t---\n1332\t\n1333\t## 11. Testing\n1334\t\n1335\t### 11.1 The one command\n1336\t`node test/run.mjs [suite ...]`, run from `<dev>`:\n1337\t- it runs every suite, or only those named;\n1338\t- it prints **only failures**, as `FAIL <suite> › <case>: <detail>`;\n1339\t- then one line: `142 passed, 0 failed (14 suites, 63.4 s)`;\n1340\t- the exit code is 1 on any failure.\n1341\t\n1342\tBrowser suites need `cd engine && npm install && npx playwright install chromium` once. Our suites load Playwright from `engine/node_modules` (`createRequire(new URL('../engine/package.json', import.meta.url))`), so one install serves both the engine's tools and our tests. If Playwright is missing, the runner prints that as a failure; it never skips silently.\n1343\t\n1344\tRerun only the suites covering the code you changed (`node test/run.mjs unit-ball sim-batting`).\n1345\t\n1346\t### 11.2 How the game is driven headless\n1347\t- Load `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and `dist/game.js` into a `vm` context with the stand-ins `window`, `addEventListener`, `location` and `matchMedia` (as `engine/kits/test.mjs` does), then `game = E.current`.\n1348\t- Drive with `game.advance(seconds)` (exact 1/120 s steps), `game.input.tap/hold/press/release`, and `input.feed` for the mouse. Seed `Math.random = E.rng(7)` and `MatchConfig.seed`.\n1349\t- `game.debug` (80-debug.js) provides:\n1350\t  - `snapshot()`: `{ scene, mode, ui: { device, glyphs, touchGate, prompts: [...], menuFocus }, match: { innings, runs, wkts, balls, over, target, need, freeHit, striker, nonStriker, bowler, hype: [a, b], fire, items, result }, ball: { phase, x, y, z, v, pitched, fx }, last (the last ball record), director: { state, shot }, story: { chapter, beat, flags }, attract: { active, segment }, hub: { active, phase, sent: { progress, result } }, dev: { open, changed: [...] }, coverage: {...}, errors }`;\n1351\t  - `idealPress()`: the step to press for a PERFECT on the current ball;\n1352\t  - `forceDelivery(spec)`, `forceOutcome(kind)`, `startMatch(cfg)`, `startChapter(n, beat)`, `setTuning(k, v)`, `spawnItem(id, at)`, `triggerChaos(id)`, `skipTo(state)`.\n1353\t- **The coverage tracker** marks features as they happen (each delivery family, shot family, dismissal, special, item, target, chaos event, camera shot, review, rain, fog, night, Super Over, mix-up, dive, overthrow). Bot and attract suites assert on it.\n1354\t\n1355\t### 11.3 Suites\n1356\t| Suite | What it checks |\n1357\t|---|---|\n1358\t| `unit-ball` | §5.1 tests |\n1359\t| `unit-rules` | §5.7.6 |\n1360\t| `unit-shots` | §5.3: resolver rows, timing grades, edges |\n1361\t| `unit-umpire` | §5.6 |\n1362\t| `unit-ui` | HUD layout overlap on 4 sizes; the glyph mapping for codes; line lengths after the template fill (§5.12); hub tag lengths |\n1363\t| `sim-batting` | ~12 scenarios (§5.3 tests), driven by real input at `idealPress() ± offsets` |\n1364\t| `sim-bowling` | ~8 scenarios (§5.2) |\n1365\t| `sim-running-fielding` | ~12 scenarios (§5.4, §5.5) |\n1366\t| `sim-arcade` | every special, item, target and chaos event forced once: its effect observable, no errors, the state restored afterwards |\n1367\t| `sim-front` | title → menu by keys, pad and mouse (hover and click); settings items exist; the pause menu has our items; dev mode open, slider change, reset; the About pages hold every Source Information field and the 3 feedback lists; the touch-only gate; prompts follow the device; Xbox glyph setting |\n1368\t| `sim-mp` | local players join; roles; co-op agreement and mix-up; per-player prompts |\n1369\t| `bot-match` | CPU vs CPU, 2 overs, on each of the 5 grounds and the 3 times of day. Each must finish with a result. Totals must be plausible (runs 5–90 per innings, extras < 30%). No director state may exceed its timeout, and every ball must end within 15 s. There must be no errors, and the coverage must include ≥ 1 four, ≥ 1 wicket and ≥ 1 run. |\n1370\t| `bot-campaign` | New Game → prologue → chapters 1–5 → ending → credits, all by virtual input from the autopilot. The autopilot uses the AI's judgment (no cheats) at Village difficulty, with up to 3 retries per chapter. All beats must fire in order, all goals be evaluated, the save show complete and Continue work after a reload. It also asserts the duration and that there are no errors. |\n1371\t| `attract-coverage` | §5.18 |\n1372\t| `dev` | §5.19.3 |\n1373\t| `hub-mock` | §5.17.3 |\n1374\t| `bundle` | the file name; the session client is the first script after the charset meta, identical to vendor; hub and catalogue tags are present and valid; no external URLs in `src=` or `fetch(`; no `TODO`, `FIXME` or `placeholder` in `src/`; `exit-interview.json` (when present) parses and every value is non-empty |\n1375\t| `browser-smoke` | Playwright via `engine/tools/check.mjs` on the bundle and deep links (`#match`, `#nets`, `#about`, `#dev`; implement hash deep links in `99-start.js` for tools only): no errors or engine warnings; its look notes printed as failures only if they're severe (low contrast or flat areas on the match scene). Screenshots are saved to `test/out/` |\n1376\t| `browser-hub` | §5.17.3 harness runs |\n1377\t\n1378\t### 11.4 Balance tests (run in M7; they report, not gate)\n1379\t`node test/balance.mjs` runs 200 CPU-vs-CPU balls per difficulty and per ground, and prints the run rate, wickets per over, boundary share and extras share. Targets at County: about 8–11 runs an over, about 0.6 wickets an over, extras below 10%. Tune with the dev sliders, then copy the values into the defaults.\n1380\t\n1381\t### 11.5 Screenshots and filmstrips (what scripts can't check)\n1382\tReview with your own eyes, saved under `test/out/`:\n1383\t- the title;\n1384\t- each ground in broadcast and wide (10 shots) at 427×240, plus one at 320×690 and one at 640×270;\n1385\t- each team kit (6);\n1386\t- the HUD in batting, bowling and fielding;\n1387\t- the third-umpire screen, Owl-Eye, an ON FIRE batter, each special's FX (still frames);\n1388\t- the story map, a cutscene with portraits, the results screen with its report;\n1389\t- the dev panel (legible at 10 feet: view at 1920×1080 scaled to 25%);\n1390\t- the touch-only gate and each About page;\n1391\t- filmstrips: 6 shot families, the pace and spin bowling actions, the dive, the diving catch, umpire signals OUT, FOUR and SIX.\n1392\t\n1393\t---\n1394\t\n1395\t## 12. Final delivery checklist\n1396\t- [ ] `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174825.html` in the root: one file, opens from file:// to the title, no network requests, and the AI Hub client is the first script in `<head>`.\n1397\t- [ ] Every feature in §5 is present and reachable in play: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n1398\t- [ ] Attract mode after 10 s idle on the title and menus; any input exits.\n1399\t- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu: live sliders with reset to defaults, toggles and jumps.\n1400\t- [ ] AI Hub: the harness passes for 1, 2 and 4 players, and the game runs standalone outside a session.\n1401\t- [ ] Controller-first 10-foot UI; keyboard and mouse native; prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs, with Xbox in Settings; the touch-only gate.\n1402\t- [ ] All audio in code, with gibberish voices.\n1403\t- [ ] `node test/run.mjs` prints `… passed, 0 failed`.\n1404\t- [ ] The About/Credits pages and the **chat reply** both carry Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, with \"unknown\" where unconfirmed.\n1405\t- [ ] `exit-interview.json` in the root: the exact shape from TASK.md, parses as JSON, every value filled.\n1406\t- [ ] `engine/CHANGES-KERFUFFLE.md` lists the engine changes, and the Engine Feedback answers name them.\n1407\t- [ ] All processes you started are stopped by PID.\n1408\t\n1409\t---\n1410\t\n1411\t## 13. Where each TASK.md requirement is met\n1412\t| TASK.md requirement | Plan |\n1413\t|---|---|\n1414\t| Genre and perspective chosen to fit cricket (over-the-top arcade) | §2, §5.11 |\n1415\t| Title: a riff on the name, 50 brainstormed, picked by a real RNG | header |\n1416\t| Single HTML file, named as given | §1.1, §3.6 |\n1417\t| Build on the my-3d2dge handoff; free to change the engine | §1.2, §3.1, §3.5 |\n1418\t| Engine's native style plus new source-specific art | §6 |\n1419\t| Engine's native animation plus new animations | §7 |\n1420\t| All audio in code, with gibberish voices | §5.13 |\n1421\t| Online: AI Hub lib/hub, and the game on its own | §5.17, §5.16.5 |\n1422\t| Dev subfolder and bundling; file:// preferred; servers on port 0; PID-only stops | §1.2, §3.2, §3.6, §11 |\n1423\t| Performance budget unlimited | §1.3, §6 |\n1424\t| Headless testing with game.advance and game.debug, a scripted full playthrough, one command with failures and a count | §11 |\n1425\t| A feature-complete vertical slice that captures the source's world, characters, themes and tone | §2, §8 |\n1426\t| Dev mode from pause, live sliders and reset | §5.19 |\n1427\t| Attract mode after 10 s idle; any input exits; AI may cheat | §5.18 |\n1428\t| Multiplayer | §5.16.5, §5.17 |\n1429\t| Narrative tone like the source's | §5.12, §8.8, §8.9 |\n1430\t| 10-foot controller-first UI; native keyboard and mouse; hover focus; device-following prompts; PS glyphs with an Xbox option; no dense data screens | §5.14, §5.15 |\n1431\t| Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\", the settings button, attract runs | §5.15.6 |\n1432\t| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §1.3, §11.3 (the bundle grep), §12 |\n1433\t| Source Information and feedback in the chat reply and an About/Credits screen | §5.21, §12 |\n1434\t| exit-interview.json in the exact shape | §5.21, §11.3, §12 |\n1435\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17695eeb-ca5d-4805-90b6-169496893b17","uuid":"d79ba429-d362-474b-baa1-0d98157f7952","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:21:47.800Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-062125__xe36ddc/work/PLAN.md","content":"- the tide: the sea-side boundary moves in a step at each over's start (the ellipse's sea-side radius shrinks, up to 15% over the innings). **Don't re-bake the floor for it.** Draw the advancing water edge and the moved rope as animated `r.decal` bands over the baked sand, and tag wet sand logically (a y threshold) for the slower outfield;\n- the rain delay (scripted in chapter 4; available in Quick Match weather \"rain\"): rain, covers, tea scene, the Kerfuffle Method;\n- dust devils: deflect aerial balls passing through ±10°;\n- rabbits: cosmetic;\n- fog banks: change the fog density over 2 overs;\n- ghost phasing: a ghost fielder is intangible for 0.5 s at random;\n- fireworks: on sixes at night;\n- the advert break: a 3 s card between overs at the Megadome;\n- the mascot pitch invader: a chicken costume, chased by stewards; cosmetic, 1 over, any ground in Quick Match with Kerfuffle rules.\n\n### 8.8 Story: *The Grand Kerfuffle* (5 chapters)\nThe writing style is dry, affectionate and digressive, like the commentary box; short lines; no line over 2 × 42 characters; markup for comic timing (`{w=.5}`, `{shake}`).\n\n**Prologue** (cutscene on the village green at dawn, after New Game):\n- AUBREY (narrating, as *The Kerfuffle Almanack*): \"Kerfuffle-on-the-Wold. Population: two hundred and twelve, and a cow called Doris.\"\n- AUBREY: \"Nothing of note has happened here since the hailstorm of 1953,{w=.4} which was rained off.\"\n- *The Phantom crunches across the square. Tyre marks on the pitch. Mrs Crumb drops a scone.*\n- THRUMPTON: \"Fourth of June, 1975. First ball. Given out leg before by a vicar{w=.3} who was looking at a butterfly.\"\n- EDIE: \"That was my grandfather. He still talks about that butterfly.\"\n- THRUMPTON: \"I have purchased the deeds to this green. On Monday it becomes the Thrumpton Parking Plaza.{w=.3} Four hundred spaces.{w=.3} No cricket.\"\n- MRS CRUMB: \"Over my dead sponge.\"\n- THRUMPTON: \"Unless... you beat my teams in the Grand Kerfuffle. Five matches. My grounds. My rules.{w=.3} Your umpires. I'm not a monster.\"\n- EDIE: \"Done. We'll play you anywhere.{w=.3} Bring cake.\"\n- *Title card: THE GRAND KERFUFFLE.*\n\n| # | Chapter | Opponent · ground | Scenario | Teaches | Beats | Kerfuffle Goals (stars) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **A Gentle Knock** | Lower Muddleford · Village Green | full match, 2 overs each, KER bats first, at the player's difficulty (Muddleford are the weakest side, so it plays gently) | Nets lessons 1–4 and 6: aim, ground, loft, defend, run, bowl | pre: Gaz's challenge (\"by warm-up I mean a thrashing\"); Nets with Mrs Crumb (\"Watch the ball, dear, not the cake\"); after innings 1: Thrumpton watches from the car (\"With the heater on\"); win: \"Beginner's luck. Thrumpton Hall next. Dress code: impeccable.\" | win · smash the pub window · hit a six |\n| 2 | **Tea on the Lawn** | Gentlemen of Thrumpton · Thrumpton Hall (overcast) | \"Kerfuffle posted 24 after a top-order collapse, chiefly due to peacocks.\" The Gentlemen need 25 from 2 overs: **you bowl and field** | lessons 7–11: aftertouch, Hype specials, catch ring, throws, reviews (the KRS appears) | pre: Peregrine (\"Do mind the peacocks; they bite\"); Fortescue announces tea \"at the fall of the third wicket, or at four, whichever is more dignified\"; mid: the ball comes back sticky (\"Is that... marmalade?\"), a review tutorial; win: \"I shall have Fortescue polish your trophy. With marmalade.\" | win · take a PERFECT-ring catch · win a review |\n| 3 | **Sand in the Sandwiches** | Sunburnt Bay Larrikins · Sunburnt Bay | chase 30 from 2 overs vs pace: **you bat** | bouncers (duck, hook), hard running and the dive, the tide | pre: the minibus breaks down and the team pushes it (\"Statistically, sunscreen doesn't melt at—\" / \"Mate.\"); mid: the tide warning; win: Shazza warns \"He's been buying ringers. Weird ones. See-through ones.\" | win · hook a six · win with a dive making the crease |\n| 4 | **Now You See It** | Magic Circle XI · Dustbowl Downs | full match, 2 overs each; a rain delay in innings 2, the Kerfuffle Method | spin (lesson 5: charge), stumpings, the rain delay, tea treats | pre: Spinaldo (\"Pick a card. It will be the card of your downfall.\"), Basil (\"I bowled leg-spin to a magician once. He sawed my stumps in half.\"); mid: rain, covers, the tea room scene, Mrs Crumb's chalkboard (\"carry the scone...\"); win: Spinaldo reveals the ghosts and the midnight booking | win · stump a batter · hit the hot-air balloon |\n| 5 | **The Midnight Final** | Thrumpton's Thunderbolts · The Megadome (night, fog) | full match, 3 overs each; the final over of the KER chase is the Thrumptonator's boss over; a Super Over if tied | ON FIRE emphasis, Triple Threat, ghosts, fog, the Super Over | pre: the Megadome (\"No tea. No cake. No interval. Just ADVERTS.\"); the ghosts rise (\"We have waited one hundred and forty-four years for a match that wasn't rained off.\" / EDIE: \"Then let's give you one.\"); mid: fog rolls in; the Thrumptonator wheeled out (\"Steam-powered. Never misses. Never gives anyone out leg before on a butterfly.\"); **win ending:** Thrumpton demands one exhibition ball against Rev. Hollis, who gives him out LBW first ball, again. Thrumpton laughs for the first time in 51 years: \"Plumb. Absolutely plumb.\" He tears up the deeds, the ghosts depart in peace (\"Worth the wait.\"), and the Almanack closes: \"Lord Thrumpton-Vane now polishes the tea urn on Saturdays and is said to be adequate at fine leg.\" Then credits. | win · survive the Thrumptonator's over without losing a wicket · hit the jumbotron |\n\n**Losses** (every chapter): a short consolation, e.g. MRS CRUMB: \"Never mind, dear. Even the best of us get a golden duck. Have a scone and go again.\" Then Retry / Retry on Village / Map.\n\nThe beats run as `game.script` generators on the bus (for example, `yield E.until(() => match.innings === 1 && match.phase === 'between')`, then play the scene). Story scene data goes through `E.Story` nodes, with speakers mapped to portraits.\n\n### 8.9 Lines\n#### 8.9.1 Commentary starter set (write ≥ 3 per event per commentator in this voice; A = Aubrey, D = Dazza)\n- **match start:** A \"Good afternoon from {ground}, where the sun is out, the tea is stewed, and {team} are about to play cricket, after a fashion.\" D \"Should be a cracker. Or a shambles. Probably both.\"\n- **dot:** A \"Defended. A stroke of great dignity and no ambition whatsoever.\" D \"Nothing doing.\" A \"Left alone. The ball goes by like a gossip past a closed door.\"\n- **beaten:** A \"Beaten all ends up! He could not have missed that more if he'd brought a map.\" D \"Played and missed. Dreadful. Lovely ball, mind.\"\n- **single:** D \"Tip and run.\" A \"A quick single, taken with all the urgency of a vicar late for a fête.\"\n- **four:** A \"FOUR! Struck with the elegance of a swan, and the violence of an angry swan.\" D \"Too short, too wide, too bad. Four.\"\n- **six:** A \"That is MAXIMUM! Somebody alert the air-traffic people.\" D \"That's gone into the next postcode, mate.\"\n- **six into the pub:** A \"Through the window of the Leaning Wicket! Last orders, I fear, have been called by the ball.\"\n- **greenhouse:** A \"Into the vicarage greenhouse. There goes the marrow competition.\"\n- **bowled:** A \"Bowled him! The stumps are doing cartwheels, which is more than the batsman managed.\" D \"Timber!\"\n- **caught:** D \"Up, up... and taken. Safe as houses.\" A \"A catch of quiet magnificence. Someone get that fielder a scone.\"\n- **dropped:** A \"Dropped! Butter, I think, would have had a firmer grip.\" D \"Oh, he'll be buying the drinks tonight.\"\n- **LBW:** A \"A huge appeal! The Reverend raises... raises... yes, eventually, the finger.\" D \"Plumb. Plumber than a plumber.\"\n- **run out:** A \"Yes! No! Wait! Sorry! The four stages of grief, conducted at a sprint.\" D \"Run out by a country mile.\"\n- **stumped:** A \"Down the pitch, through the gate, and the bails are off before you can say Kerfuffle.\"\n- **wide:** D \"Wide. Wide enough to land a plane.\"\n- **no-ball:** A \"No-ball! He's overstepped, which in this village is practically a felony. Free hit to come.\"\n- **ON FIRE:** D \"The bat is literally smoking. Someone fetch a bucket.\" A \"Willow ablaze! Health and Safety will want a word.\"\n- **special:** A \"Oh, he's going for something special. I can't look. I'm looking.\"\n- **review:** PRIYA \"Owl-Eye has it... pitching in line... hitting... and it's clipping the bails by a whisker of a whisker.\"\n- **rain:** A \"And down it comes. The covers are on, the umbrellas are up, and the crowd are discussing the weather, which is the only thing they love more than cricket.\"\n- **the cow:** A \"There's a cow on the outfield. A Friesian, I believe. She's at deep midwicket and, frankly, better positioned than their fine leg.\"\n- **idle filler:** A \"A Mrs Hepplewhite of Lower Muddleford has sent in a lemon drizzle. Mrs Hepplewhite, you are a saint.\" A \"There's a pigeon at short leg who has, I think, been there since Tuesday.\" D \"Lovely day for it.\" A \"Is it? I hadn't noticed. I've been looking at this cake.\"\n- **win:** A \"And that's the match! Victory for {winner}, for common sense, and for the scone.\" **loss:** D \"That's that, then. Shake hands, have a sandwich, try again.\"\n\n#### 8.9.2 Shouts (gibberish voice, captions in speech bubbles)\n\"YES!\", \"NO!\", \"WAIT!\", \"TWO!\", \"HOWZAT!\", \"OUT!\", \"CATCH IT!\", \"MINE!\", \"SORRY!\", and the crowd's \"KER-FUF-FLE!\".\n\n#### 8.9.3 Match report templates (results screen; fill from the ball records; pick by the shape of the result)\n- \"{winner}, set {target}, were indebted to {topBat} ({topRuns}{notOut}, {sixes} sixes, one of them through {targetHit}). Play was held up for {delayMins} minutes while {chaosThing} was persuaded off the square.\"\n- \"{loser} never recovered from {collapse}. {topBowl} took {wkts} for {runs} with a mixture of guile, swing and, in one instance, marmalade.\"\n- \"A tie, decided by a Super Over of almost unbearable tension, at the end of which {hero} was carried from the field on the shoulders of the scorer.\"\n\n### 8.10 Music\nSee §5.13.4. Sketch each song in the notation and audition it in the Nets (a dev-mode \"Jukebox\" row on the JUMP tab plays each song and sting).\n\n---\n\n## 9. Build order and milestones\nEach milestone ends with its tests green (`node test/run.mjs`), a bundle build, and a look at the screenshots it touched. Commit nothing outside `<dev>` except the final .html and the exit interview.\n\n| M | Name | Builds | Exit criteria |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **M0** | Scaffold | the dev folder; the engine copied; vendor hub files; `tools/build.mjs` producing `dist/` and the single-file bundle with the client first; `test/run.mjs` running a first suite plus the bundle checks; `tools/serve.mjs`; a first title scene with the logo (finished in M4) | `node test/run.mjs` prints `N passed, 0 failed`; the bundle opens from file:// to the title; `engine/tools/check.mjs` passes on the bundle |\n| **M1** | **The Nets spike (feel first)** | the Village Green TileMap (basic floor texture), the broadcast and wide views; the batter rig with the **bat** (engine change 1) and pads; the bowling machine; the ball physics and predictor; the timing model and ground, loft and block shots for 6 resolver rows; the shadow, pitch marker and timing words; the cut to the wide cam; boundary detection (4 and 6); the TUNING registry and a minimal dev panel (sliders only) | unit-ball and unit-shots green; filmstrips of 3 shots and the bowling machine look right; a human can hit PERFECT drives reliably after 10 balls on County (play it) |\n| **M2** | Match loop | rules (§5.7), the delivery director, running (§5.4) with the AI partner, fielding (§5.5) for the CPU side, umpire decisions and signals (bowled, caught, LBW, run out, stumped), innings, target, result, toss, Super Over; the CPU batting and bowling AI; Quick Match 1P vs CPU with the human batting and the CPU bowling | unit-rules and unit-umpire green; sim scenarios for running, wickets and boundaries green; **bot-match** (CPU vs CPU, Village Green) completes with a result and no stuck balls |\n| **M3** | Human bowling and fielding, and the hub early | §5.2 in full (panel, marker, meter, aftertouch, over/round, field presets), catch ring, throws, keeper, bowler select, captain AI; **AI Hub parallel Super Over** (§5.17) with our card | sim scenarios for bowling, catching and throws green; **hub-mock** green; **browser-hub** passes with 1, 2 and 4 players (latency and loss); a full 1P Quick Match playable in both roles |\n| **M4** | Presentation | the camera director (all shots) and the close and review views; the recorder, replays, Owl-Eye, the third umpire and KRS; the HUD (§5.15.2); glyph prompts (§5.14.3, engine change 4); front-end menus, setup and pause items; settings; the 10-foot layout; the touch-only gate; commentary with captions; the gibberish voice synth (engine change 3); SFX, the crowd engine, music with layers | prompt and glyph tests green; HUD layout tests green on 4 sizes; browser smoke screenshots reviewed; commentary tests green |\n| **M5** | The arcade layer | Hype, ON FIRE, every special (§8.6), items, tea treats, stadium targets, chaos events, weather and time of day (fog, night lights), difficulty levels | sim scenarios for each special, item, target and chaos event green (forced via debug) |\n| **M6** | Content | all 5 grounds with their art (§6.3, §6.5), panoramas, props and palettes; the 6 teams and 66 players with rigs, portraits and voices; the story map, the 5 chapters, cutscenes, beats, goals and stars, the endings; the Nets lessons and Six Machine; Showdown Bat and Bowl with tables; Versus with 2–4 players; saves, unlocks; Wisden-style reports; all music | **bot-campaign** completes the story; bot-match on all grounds; local MP tests green; screenshots of every ground and kit reviewed |\n| **M7** | Attract, dev, about, polish | the attract showreel (10 segments) and its coverage; the full dev panel (4 tabs, every toggle and action); About/Credits pages; engine changes logged; balance passes with the dev sliders (aim: a County CPU chase of 30 off 2 overs succeeds about 50% vs a competent human); final bundle; exit-interview.json | **all suites green**, including attract-coverage, dev, bundle and the browser hub runs; no TODO or FIXME strings in `src/` (a test greps for them); the final reply written |\n\nWork inside each milestone in this order: simulation (with unit tests), then presentation, then scenario tests, then screenshots.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Risks and how to de-risk them\n\n| # | Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk now | Complete fallback if it fails |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Batting feel and readability** in an orthographic view | the depth and height of a fast ball are ambiguous without perspective; batting is the game | M1 first: the shadow disc, the pitch marker, the trail and length bands; the timing words; tune `camPitch`, `camScale`, `ballSpeed` and the windows with dev sliders; human playtest after M1 | raise the pitch marker to always-on with a closing timing ring (Statistical Certainty's visual) as the default \"Classic\" assist |\n| 2 | **Bat and two-handed shots on the rig** | the engine rig has swords, not bats; two-handed IK in the draw pose could fight the attack specs | engine change 1 in M1 plus a filmstrip of each shot family; put the left hand on the handle by IK *after* the attack pose; keep `hand: 'both'` specs | a one-handed bat hold (the left hand following loosely), which still reads as a bat at 40 px |\n| 3 | **Bowling action (windmill)** | there's no stock move for a vertical overarm arc | `solvePose` post-processing with an `E.ik3` circle over 0.18 s; filmstrip; compare with the `throw` move | the engine's `throw` move with a higher `z1` and a hop, which reads as overarm |\n| 4 | **Physics, predictor and AI coherence** | the AI, LBW, catches and Owl-Eye all depend on the predictor matching reality | one step function shared by the sim and the predictor; no randomness inside it (the seam deviation is stored at release); unit test the match within 0.01 units | the AI and fielders read a simpler ballistic prediction, and LBW and Owl-Eye use the recorded real path up to impact plus a ballistic continuation from it |\n| 5 | **Floor baking with big grounds and several views** | each view and scale bakes the floor; the cache clears past 6; zoom tweens re-bake | fixed views (no zoom tweens), raise the limit to 10 (engine change 6), warm the bakes in boot, chunked bakes; instrument `map.floors` | smaller grounds (rx 520) and only 3 views (close becomes broadcast with a tighter focus) |\n| 6 | **Stalled deliveries** (a fielder never reaches the ball, a ball never settles) | a stuck game is game-breaking | a timeout on every director state; the 15 s inPlay cap; the bot-match stuck check | already complete: the timeouts are the fallback |\n| 7 | **AI Hub conformance** | the client must come first; no blur pause; ready with no key; Enter on our card; time-up and end handling | M3 early; harness runs in the test command; `autoPause: false` in sessions; `card: true` handled with keys, pad and clicks | use the hub's own card (`card: false`), which removes the Enter check |\n| 8 | **Content volume** (5 grounds, 6 teams, story, lines) | it can crowd out polish | data registries plus the ground recipe builder; a squad generator; stars hand-made only; content in M6 after systems are final | fewer props per ground and shorter line pools (≥ 3 per event), never fewer grounds or chapters |\n| 9 | **Gibberish voice quality and clipping** | many simultaneous syllables could clip or sound harsh | a voice bus with a compressor (`DynamicsCompressorNode`); max 2 voices at once (queue); audition in the dev Jukebox | simpler square-blip voices with per-speaker pitch, still gibberish |\n| 10 | **The attract mode looping forever without errors** | long unattended runs find rare bugs | it uses the real machinery with cheats; the attract-coverage test runs 12 minutes; `game.errors` stays empty | fewer segments (keep ≥ 6, covering the coverage list) |\n| 11 | **Input conflicts** (J/K/L confirm and cancel, hub Create + Options, rebinding) | wrong menu behaviour annoys at once | a custom preset with confirm J and cancel L; engine change 5; tests for prompts and rebinding | — |\n| 12 | **Bundle size or an inline `</script>`** | a broken single file is a broken deliverable | the build escapes it, then a bundle test opens the bundle headless and in a browser | — |\n\n---\n\n## 11. Testing\n\n### 11.1 The one command\n`node test/run.mjs [suite ...]`, run from `<dev>`:\n- it runs every suite, or only those named;\n- it prints **only failures**, as `FAIL <suite> › <case>: <detail>`;\n- then one line: `142 passed, 0 failed (14 suites, 63.4 s)`;\n- the exit code is 1 on any failure.\n\nBrowser suites need `cd engine && npm install && npx playwright install chromium` once. Our suites load Playwright from `engine/node_modules` (`createRequire(new URL('../engine/package.json', import.meta.url))`), so one install serves both the engine's tools and our tests. If Playwright is missing, the runner prints that as a failure; it never skips silently.\n\nRerun only the suites covering the code you changed (`node test/run.mjs unit-ball sim-batting`).\n\n### 11.2 How the game is driven headless\n- Load `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and `dist/game.js` into a `vm` context with the stand-ins `window`, `addEventListener`, `location` and `matchMedia` (as `engine/kits/test.mjs` does), then `game = E.current`.\n- Drive with `game.advance(seconds)` (exact 1/120 s steps), `game.input.tap/hold/press/release`, and `input.feed` for the mouse. Seed `Math.random = E.rng(7)` and `MatchConfig.seed`.\n- `game.debug` (80-debug.js) provides:\n  - `snapshot()`: `{ scene, mode, ui: { device, glyphs, touchGate, prompts: [...], menuFocus }, match: { innings, runs, wkts, balls, over, target, need, freeHit, striker, nonStriker, bowler, hype: [a, b], fire, items, result }, ball: { phase, x, y, z, v, pitched, fx }, last (the last ball record), director: { state, shot }, story: { chapter, beat, flags }, attract: { active, segment }, hub: { active, phase, sent: { progress, result } }, dev: { open, changed: [...] }, coverage: {...}, errors }`;\n  - `idealPress()`: the step to press for a PERFECT on the current ball;\n  - `forceDelivery(spec)`, `forceOutcome(kind)`, `startMatch(cfg)`, `startChapter(n, beat)`, `setTuning(k, v)`, `spawnItem(id, at)`, `triggerChaos(id)`, `skipTo(state)`.\n- **The coverage tracker** marks features as they happen (each delivery family, shot family, dismissal, special, item, target, chaos event, camera shot, review, rain, fog, night, Super Over, mix-up, dive, overthrow). Bot and attract suites assert on it.\n\n### 11.3 Suites\n| Suite | What it checks |\n|---|---|\n| `unit-ball` | §5.1 tests |\n| `unit-rules` | §5.7.6 |\n| `unit-shots` | §5.3: resolver rows, timing grades, edges |\n| `unit-umpire` | §5.6 |\n| `unit-ui` | HUD layout overlap on 4 sizes; the glyph mapping for codes; line lengths after the template fill (§5.12); hub tag lengths |\n| `sim-batting` | ~12 scenarios (§5.3 tests), driven by real input at `idealPress() ± offsets` |\n| `sim-bowling` | ~8 scenarios (§5.2) |\n| `sim-running-fielding` | ~12 scenarios (§5.4, §5.5) |\n| `sim-arcade` | every special, item, target and chaos event forced once: its effect observable, no errors, the state restored afterwards |\n| `sim-front` | title → menu by keys, pad and mouse (hover and click); settings items exist; the pause menu has our items; dev mode open, slider change, reset; the About pages hold every Source Information field and the 3 feedback lists; the touch-only gate; prompts follow the device; Xbox glyph setting |\n| `sim-mp` | local players join; roles; co-op agreement and mix-up; per-player prompts |\n| `bot-match` | CPU vs CPU, 2 overs, on each of the 5 grounds and the 3 times of day. Each must finish with a result. Totals must be plausible (runs 5–90 per innings, extras < 30%). No director state may exceed its timeout, and every ball must end within 15 s. There must be no errors, and the coverage must include ≥ 1 four, ≥ 1 wicket and ≥ 1 run. |\n| `bot-campaign` | New Game → prologue → chapters 1–5 → ending → credits, all by virtual input from the autopilot. The autopilot uses the AI's judgment (no cheats) at Village difficulty, with up to 3 retries per chapter. All beats must fire in order, all goals be evaluated, the save show complete and Continue work after a reload. It also asserts the duration and that there are no errors. |\n| `attract-coverage` | §5.18 |\n| `dev` | §5.19.3 |\n| `hub-mock` | §5.17.3 |\n| `bundle` | the file name; the session client is the first script after the charset meta, identical to vendor; hub and catalogue tags are present and valid; no external URLs in `src=` or `fetch(`; no `TODO`, `FIXME` or `placeholder` in `src/`; `exit-interview.json` (when present) parses and every value is non-empty |\n| `browser-smoke` | Playwright via `engine/tools/check.mjs` on the bundle and deep links (`#match`, `#nets`, `#about`, `#dev`; implement hash deep links in `99-start.js` for tools only): no errors or engine warnings; its look notes printed as failures only if they're severe (low contrast or flat areas on the match scene). Screenshots are saved to `test/out/` |\n| `browser-hub` | §5.17.3 harness runs |\n\n### 11.4 Balance tests (run in M7; they report, not gate)\n`node test/balance.mjs` runs 200 CPU-vs-CPU balls per difficulty and per ground, and prints the run rate, wickets per over, boundary share and extras share. Targets at County: about 8–11 runs an over, about 0.6 wickets an over, extras below 10%. Tune with the dev sliders, then copy the values into the defaults.\n\n### 11.5 Screenshots and filmstrips (what scripts can't check)\nReview with your own eyes, saved under `test/out/`:\n- the title;\n- each ground in broadcast and wide (10 shots) at 427×240, plus one at 320×690 and one at 640×270;\n- each team kit (6);\n- the HUD in batting, bowling and fielding;\n- the third-umpire screen, Owl-Eye, an ON FIRE batter, each special's FX (still frames);\n- the story map, a cutscene with portraits, the results screen with its report;\n- the dev panel (legible at 10 feet: view at 1920×1080 scaled to 25%);\n- the touch-only gate and each About page;\n- filmstrips: 6 shot families, the pace and spin bowling actions, the dive, the diving catch, umpire signals OUT, FOUR and SIX.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Final delivery checklist\n- [ ] `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174825.html` in the root: one file, opens from file:// to the title, no network requests, and the AI Hub client is the first script in `<head>`.\n- [ ] Every feature in §5 is present and reachable in play: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n- [ ] Attract mode after 10 s idle on the title and menus; any input exits.\n- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu: live sliders with reset to defaults, toggles and jumps.\n- [ ] AI Hub: the harness passes for 1, 2 and 4 players, and the game runs standalone outside a session.\n- [ ] Controller-first 10-foot UI; keyboard and mouse native; prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs, with Xbox in Settings; the touch-only gate.\n- [ ] All audio in code, with gibberish voices.\n- [ ] `node test/run.mjs` prints `… passed, 0 failed`.\n- [ ] The About/Credits pages and the **chat reply** both carry Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, with \"unknown\" where unconfirmed.\n- [ ] `exit-interview.json` in the root: the exact shape from TASK.md, parses as JSON, every value filled.\n- [ ] `engine/CHANGES-KERFUFFLE.md` lists the engine changes, and the Engine Feedback answers name them.\n- [ ] All processes you started are stopped by PID.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Where each TASK.md requirement is met\n| TASK.md requirement | Plan |\n|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective chosen to fit cricket (over-the-top arcade) | §2, §5.11 |\n| Title: a riff on the name, 50 brainstormed, picked by a real RNG | header |\n| Single HTML file, named as given | §1.1, §3.6 |\n| Build on the my-3d2dge handoff; free to change the engine | §1.2, §3.1, §3.5 |\n| Engine's native style plus new source-specific art | §6 |\n| Engine's native animation plus new animations | §7 |\n| All audio in code, with gibberish voices | §5.13 |\n| Online: AI Hub lib/hub, and the game on its own | §5.17, §5.16.5 |\n| Dev subfolder and bundling; file:// preferred; servers on port 0; PID-only stops | §1.2, §3.2, §3.6, §11 |\n| Performance budget unlimited | §1.3, §6 |\n| Headless testing with game.advance and game.debug, a scripted full playthrough, one command with failures and a count | §11 |\n| A feature-complete vertical slice that captures the source's world, characters, themes and tone | §2, §8 |\n| Dev mode from pause, live sliders and reset | §5.19 |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle; any input exits; AI may cheat | §5.18 |\n| Multiplayer | §5.16.5, §5.17 |\n| Narrative tone like the source's | §5.12, §8.8, §8.9 |\n| 10-foot controller-first UI; native keyboard and mouse; hover focus; device-following prompts; PS glyphs with an Xbox option; no dense data screens | §5.14, §5.15 |\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\", the settings button, attract runs | §5.15.6 |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §1.3, §11.3 (the bundle grep), §12 |\n| Source Information and feedback in the chat reply and an About/Credits screen | §5.21, §12 |\n| exit-interview.json in the exact shape | §5.21, §11.3, §12 |\n","numLines":216,"startLine":1220,"totalLines":1435}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016LmrcVMJFN7GU4pJJ6drJU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
