{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - The `/goal` text, verbatim: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\"\n   - STAGE.md: build the game TASK.md describes, following PLAN.md and using the plan's title (Cricket Kerfuffle). TASK.md wins where the two disagree. Deliver the file name and the reply sections TASK.md asks for.\n   - TASK.md requirements:\n     - **Package:** a single HTML file named `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-062125.html`; dev files in a subfolder of the same name; `exit-interview.json` in the root with the exact JSON shape.\n     - **Stack:** build on the my-3d2dge handoff (the engine may be changed); use the AI Hub lib/hub for online play.\n     - **Audio:** all in code; voices are Animalese/Simlish gibberish.\n     - **Required features:**\n       - dev mode reachable from the pause menu, with live sliders and a reset to defaults;\n       - attract mode after 10 s idle, which any input exits;\n       - multiplayer;\n       - a 10-foot, controller-first UI; PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option; prompts follow the last device;\n       - touch-only devices: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\" plus a Settings button, and the attract mode still runs;\n       - an About/Credits screen and the final reply carrying Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback;\n       - no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n     - **Testing:** headless tests behind one command that prints only failures and a count; no subagents for review.\n   - Machine and security constraints (verbatim from TASK.md):\n     - \"Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"\n     - \"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"\n     - \"Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included.\"\n     - PLAN.md: don't git clone ai-hub (5 GB).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Engine:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2.\n     - Scenes and game API: E.Game scenes, game.go (clears timers), game.advance headless, game.debug.\n     - Drawing and data: E.View custom orthographic views, TileMap with floorTex and chunks, r.queue/r.actor/r.shape/r.decal/r.overlay, px.* primitives, E.font.\n     - Characters and assets: E.Humanoid rigs with attack specs (plane 'side' vertical arcs), solvePose wrapper, shapes as data (store-format asset set E.addAssets).\n     - UI and audio: E.Dialog, E.Arcade tables, game.audio (sfx/define/music/layer/sting), game.saves autosave, game.settings, pause menu items, input actions/glyphs, game.allowJoin/addPlayer, E.mkCanvas.\n   - **AI Hub Session Protocol v1** (client 1.4.0), parallel mode:\n     - flow: connect({mode, seats: [1, 4], card: true}), ready(), progress/result, time-up/end;\n     - AIHub.rng gives identical deliveries on every copy;\n     - the harness is checked via `window.__hubCheck.pass`.\n   - **Deterministic simulation:**\n     - fixed 1/120 s steps; seeded RNG.play/RNG.cosmetic;\n     - a ball predictor equal to the simulation;\n     - the delivery director state machine with phase caps.\n   - **Testing:**\n     - Node vm contexts (test/lib.mjs load()), with `Math.random` seeded via vm.runInContext;\n     - Playwright from engine/node_modules for browser suites;\n     - the python http.server (-u, port 0) for the harness, stopped by PID.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (all under `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-062125__xe36ddc/work/`):\n   - **Deliverables in the work root:**\n     - `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-062125.html`, about 1.71 MB. The session client comes first after the charset meta; the engine and game are inlined; hub tags are in the head.\n     - `exit-interview.json`, generated by tools/exit-interview.mjs from src/58-about.js; it parses.\n   - **The engine** (`<dev>/engine/my-3d2dge.js`, modified; logged in `engine/CHANGES-KERFUFFLE.md`):\n     1. a bat weapon with a two-handed IK grip (`_drawBat`, batRest, batLen/batScale, `rig.oneHand`);\n     2. pads, a brim hat, a helmet grille, bigHands, face moustache/beard/glasses;\n     3. a voice bus plus the voiceVolume setting and `audio.bus(name)`;\n     4. the glyphs setting defaults to playstation, with options [playstation, xbox];\n     5. the hub's Create+Options (Pad8 held blocks the pause);\n     6. the floor cache raised from 6 to 10.\n   - **Build and tooling** (`<dev>/tools/`):\n     - `build.mjs`: concatenates src into dist/game.js (an IIFE), writes dist/index.html and the bundle; HUB_TAGS: session 1, players 1-4, mode parallel, minutes 2, goal, howto, type Game, players 1-4.\n     - `shot.mjs`, `serve.mjs` (python3 -u http.server, stop by PID) and `exit-interview.mjs`.\n   - **Source files** (`<dev>/src/`):\n     - Foundations: 00-head (K namespace, `scenes`), 01-const, 02-tuning, 03-rng, 04-bus, 05-store.\n     - Assets: 07-assets-kerfuffle, with 40 shapes including netPost.\n     - Data: 10-data-teams, 11-data-grounds (incl. nets netPanels), 12-data-deliveries, 13-data-shots, 14-data-specials, 15-data-arcade, 16-data-story, 17-data-lines, 18-data-music.\n     - Simulation: 20-ball, 21-rules (result uses the revised target), 22-match, 23-bowling, 24-batting, 25-play (running/fielding/netCollide), 26-umpire, 27-ai (forced outcomes, safeRun), 28-arcade.\n     - Presentation: 30-ground, 31-cast, 32-anim, 34-view (MatchView, ballVisible, gullPose, net drawing, crowd catch), 40-audio, 41-voice, 42-commentary, 43-glyphs, 44-hud (stacked callouts), 45-ui.\n     - Scenes and game: 47-game (KEYS incl. `tab: ['Tab']`, SETTINGS, the game object), 50-front, 51-attract, 53-story, 54-match, 56-modes, 58-about (ABOUT_INFO/FEEDBACK), 60-hub, 70-dev (startChapter; deferred pause lock), 80-debug (game.debug, wrapScenes, DevOverlays), 99-start.\n   - **Tests** (`<dev>/test/`):\n     - Shared: lib.mjs, run.mjs, balance.mjs.\n     - Unit: unit-ball, unit-rules, unit-shots, unit-umpire, unit-ui.\n     - Simulation: sim-batting, sim-bowling, sim-running-fielding, sim-arcade, sim-front, sim-mp, sim-extras.\n     - Long-running: bot-match, bot-campaign, attract-coverage.\n     - Other: dev, hub-mock, bundle, requirements.\n     - Browser: browser-smoke, browser-hub, browser-features.\n     - That is 22 suites.\n   - **Notes:** `<dev>/DESIGN-NOTES.md` explains how to add content.\n\n4. Errors and fixes (main ones):\n   - **Solver and timing:** the solver's pitch point was off by up to 3 units (now interpolated); the catch ring was judged 20 ms early (now the ball is held through the window).\n   - **Running:** a run was counted when both batters were sent back (crossings now track `b.from`); singles were impossible (runSpeed raised to 140 and ring fielders moved ×1.3 deeper).\n   - **Bowling and players:** the bowler released mid run-up (the meter now locks the grade and the ball is released at the crease); the keeper could be picked to bowl (fixed in buildTeam).\n   - **Stalls:** the hold never counted down in setup; the cow blocked the chaser.\n   - **Rules and difficulty:** the result ignored the Kerfuffle Method target; difficulty multipliers hit the autopilot (raw tuning is now used for human sides); seeds came from Date.now (now Math.random).\n   - **Story and grounds:** the chapter 3 target was eased to 26; the Downs turn was set to 1.3.\n   - **Forced outcomes:** lines now account for handedness, straight balls and replanning after force; forced sixes now carry the rope distance plus 70.\n   - **Throws and stands:** throws from behind the stumps counted as missed shies (fixed with th.side); stand heights are now graded.\n   - **Presentation:** palm and cactus are drawn as props; the toss crash (empty actor arrays); deep links scheduled after game.go; glyph chars missing from the font; dev-mode Space ran the row (a tab switch now returns); Escape paused under dev (deferred pausable lock); dev tabs collided with the corner buttons.\n   - **No-op row:** the dev \"...at beat\" row did nothing; fixed.\n   - **Stop hook feedback:**\n     - The hook rejected 4 times: the timeline, simplified features, unverified features, and hardware.\n     - Responses: implemented crowd catch, seagulls, fog-hidden ball and nets; added the browser-features, requirements and sim-extras suites; ran 10-foot legibility screenshots.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Every TASK.md feature is implemented and tested. The final full run passed 532 checks, 0 failed, in 22 suites.\n   - It ran after the last source and text edit, followed by a regenerated exit interview.\n   - No http.server that I started is still running (verified by cwd).\n   - Physical touch-device and gamepad testing is impossible in this environment; Playwright touch emulation and engine input injection were used instead.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The `/goal` command with the condition text quoted above.\n   - Stop hook feedback 1: the About check failing was never resolved; the feedback was not validated; simplified items (crowd catches, seagull drawing, fog hiding distant balls, Nets net walls) mean the condition is not met.\n   - Stop hook feedback 2: the transcript doesn't show every feature verified; it disputes the About timeline; the Hall art, dev panel and touch gate on hardware were checked only headlessly or with screenshots.\n   - Stop hook feedback 3: verification still insufficient; \"no stubs\" rests on a grep.\n   - Stop hook feedback 4 (latest): touch was checked only in emulation with no hardware; AI Hub only via the harness; \"no stubs\" rests on grep plus a same-session suite; the About timeline has already been rejected twice. Its final line, verbatim: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\"\n   - Several \"The user hasn't heard from you in a while\" system nudges, which were answered with brief status updates.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - None beyond satisfying the Stop hook.\n   - All deliverables exist and are verified.\n   - Remaining hook objections are physical hardware testing (impossible here) and \"independent evidence\" (not available in this environment).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - The last action was a 10-foot legibility check: `test/out/tenfoot.png`, 1920×1080 frames of the dev panel and Thrumpton Hall viewed at 25%; everything was legible.\n   - .scratch was removed; the deliverables were confirmed unchanged and `exit-interview.json` parses.\n   - The final reply restated the four sections:\n     - Usage: \"Session time about 2 h 55 min by the system clock (06:21 to about 09:15); tokens and cost unknown\".\n     - Testing feedback 1 begins \"About 40 issues across 22 suites (532 checks)...\".\n   - The latest hook again rejected and now requires a text-only summary response.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - No further code work is required. All deliverables are complete and the final te