{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011UmhCFDhfRVe4zo4x61QPf","type":"tool_result","content":"Title > the title is Cricket Kerfuffle (a riff on \"cricket\"), chosen from 50 by secrets.randbelow\nTitle > the title screen shows CRICKET KERFUFFLE\nPackage > the single file has the exact name, in the folder beside TASK.md\nPackage > everything is inlined: no external script or stylesheet\nTech > the bundle carries my-3D2dge v0.85.2\nTech > the engine changes are logged (6 numbered changes)\nArt > a new shape set of 40 cricket and ground objects is loaded\nArt > every new shape is used in the game\nArt > five grounds with their own palettes and stands\nArt > six teams of eleven in their own kits\nArt > cricket gear in the engine: bat, pads, brim hat, helmet grille\nAnimation > strokes, the bowling windmill, a spinner's arm and the keeper's stumping are specs\nAnimation > every shot family has its stroke\nAnimation > the umpire signals all ten (OUT, FOUR, SIX, WIDE, NO BALL, BYE, LEG BYE, FREE HIT, REVIEW, DEAD BALL)\nAudio > no audio files: no audio data, file extensions or Audio elements\nAudio > every sound the game plays is defined\nAudio > every sound defined is played\nAudio > 10 original songs and 11 stings, every note token valid\nAudio > every song and sting is used\nAudio > gibberish voices: \"Howzat!\" is two syllables, a question rises at its end\nAudio > every story speaker has a voice profile\nOnline > the AI Hub tag hub:session\nOnline > the AI Hub tag hub:session-players\nOnline > the AI Hub tag hub:session-mode\nOnline > the AI Hub tag hub:session-goal\nOnline > the AI Hub tag hub:session-howto\nOnline > the session client is pasted unmodified as the first script\nOnline > a session never sends (parallel mode)\nMultiplayer > a second player joins on one machine (and up to four in Versus)\nScope > every delivery in the catalogue is bowled (19)\nScope > every shot in the catalogue can be played (20)\nScope > a bowler with no special of his own bowls the Kerfuffle Ball\nScope > a batter with no special of his own plays the Kerfuffle Shot\nScope > every special belongs to a character or is a generic one (21)\nScope > every item has its effect in the rules\nScope > every chaos event is in a ground's pool or the story\nScope > five chapters, each with a pre-match scene, a win scene and three goals\nScope > eleven Nets lessons, each with a goal the lesson counts\nScope > every story scene is played somewhere\nScope > the modes: Story, Quick Match, Versus, Showdown, Nets, the attract mode and AI Hub rounds are scenes\nDev mode > the pause menu has a Dev Mode item\nDev mode > the TUNING tab has a live slider for every key gameplay variable (32)\nDev mode > Reset all to defaults restores every value\nDev mode > toggles, jumps and an info page\nAttract > after 10 s without input on the title the attract mode plays\nAttract > any input leaves it\nAttract > ten segments, with cheating autopilots on both sides\nNarrative > a commentary box in the source's voice: Sir Aubrey and Dazza, 150+ lines\nNarrative > Wisden-style match reports and a story told in scenes\nUI > the main menu has six items or fewer\nUI > keyboard: J, K, L, I, Space, Shift and E are the shot, loft, block, special, run, back and charge keys\nUI > mouse: left click hits, right click lofts; the pointer aims\nUI > the pad: PlayStation glyphs by default\nUI > the Xbox (A B X Y) setting\nUI > hover moves the focus and clicks pick in the 10-foot lists and cards\nTouch > a touch-only device sees \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button\nTouch > no scene declares touch buttons\nAbout > an in-game About/Credits screen with Source Information and the three feedback sections\nAbout > the About pages and exit-interview.json say the same\nDone > no TODO, FIXME, placeholder, lorem ipsum or \"not implemented\" in the source\nDone > no empty handlers or functions in the game code\nDone > no errors anywhere in this run\n63 p